1
00:00:03,630 --> 00:00:04,310
Alors ?
So?

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:05,150
Nathan.
Nathan.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,020
Je confirme, ça a bien été photocopié ici.
I can confirm, it was photocopied here.

4
00:00:11,340 --> 00:00:12,120
Je savais ça.
I knew that.

5
00:00:13,070 --> 00:00:16,730
Alors, c'était le mardi 22 à minuit 14 très exactement.
So, it was Tuesday the 22nd at exactly 12:14 AM.

6
00:00:18,300 --> 00:00:19,640
On peut savoir par qui ?
Can we find out by whom?

7
00:00:19,640 --> 00:00:21,620
Bah non, on n'est pas dans les experts là.
No, we're not on CSI here.

8
00:00:22,530 --> 00:00:25,530
Ce que je peux faire par contre, c'est voir les postes qui étaient allumés ce soir-là,
What I can do, though, is check which workstations were on that night,

9
00:00:25,630 --> 00:00:27,070
et les connexions au wifi aussi.
and the wifi connections too.

10
00:00:27,270 --> 00:00:27,630
Ah bah oui.
Oh yeah, sure.

11
00:00:27,830 --> 00:00:28,090
Ouais.
Yeah.

12
00:00:28,550 --> 00:00:28,950
Ok.
Ok.

13
00:00:30,010 --> 00:00:38,330
Alors, le mardi 22 à minuit, une seule connexion, un seul utilisateur.
So, Tuesday the 22nd at midnight, one connection, one user.

14
00:00:38,670 --> 00:00:58,280
Vous me prévenez quand il arrive.
Let me know when he arrives.

15
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:00,020
C'est le pompier péromène quoi.
He's a classic arsonist firefighter.

16
00:01:00,860 --> 00:01:03,760
C'est le mec qui fous le feu exprès pour se faire ensuite passer pour un sauveur.
The guy who sets the fire himself just to play the hero afterward.

17
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:08,160
Non mais dire qu'il m'amène au cimetière sur la tombe de Samuel, genre on est une grande famille quoi.
I mean, he takes me to the cemetery to Samuel's grave, acting like we're all one big family.

18
00:01:08,320 --> 00:01:10,760
Bah et moi, il vient à la maternité, il me dit que ma fille c'est un bébé ASK.
And me — he shows up at the maternity ward and tells me my daughter is an ASK baby.

19
00:01:11,220 --> 00:01:12,060
Bah qu'il a peur de rien.
Well, he's got no shame.

20
00:01:12,540 --> 00:01:13,200
Je vais me le faire.
I'm going to deal with him.

21
00:01:13,840 --> 00:01:14,840
Tu vas rien faire du tout.
You're not going to do anything.

22
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:15,220
Ah ouais ?
Oh yeah?

23
00:01:15,220 --> 00:01:15,680
Non.
No.

24
00:01:16,540 --> 00:01:18,020
On sait pas encore ce qu'il a dans la tête.
We don't know yet what he's got in mind.

25
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:19,910
Il va nous dire quoi ?
What's he going to tell us?

26
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:23,160
Et comment il compte s'en tirer avec les américains, hein ?
And how does he plan to get away with it with the Americans, huh?

27
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:26,240
Alors pour l'instant, on se tait et on observe la bête.
For now, we stay quiet and we watch the beast.

28
00:01:26,320 --> 00:01:27,020
Ouais, je suis d'accord.
Yeah, agreed.

29
00:01:27,280 --> 00:01:28,940
Gabriel, tu prends sur toi, d'accord ?
Gabriel, keep it together, alright?

30
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:29,560
Ouais, ok, ouais.
Yeah, ok, yeah.

31
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:32,500
Mais quoi ? Jeanne, il va nous rendre cette espèce d'ordure ?
But what — Jeanne, is he going to hand us back that piece of trash?

32
00:01:32,820 --> 00:01:34,380
Bon bah, bonne journée messieurs-dames, au revoir.
Well then, have a good day everyone, goodbye.

33
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:34,980
Bonne journée.
Good day.

34
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:40,700
Vous avez vu l'inscription là en bas ?
Did you see the graffiti down there?

35
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:41,760
Je suis consterné.
I'm appalled.

36
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:44,620
Le jour des 30 ans d'ASK, on avait vraiment besoin de ça.
On ASK's 30th anniversary, we really didn't need this.

37
00:01:44,920 --> 00:01:46,420
Qu'est-ce qu'elle a foutu, Camille ?
What did Camille do?

38
00:01:46,740 --> 00:01:48,860
Bon pis alors, elle doit être coincée dans le métro, là.
Come on, she's probably stuck on the metro.

39
00:01:49,100 --> 00:01:50,720
Franchement, il y a des gens, on se demande...
Honestly, some people, you really have to wonder...

40
00:01:53,260 --> 00:02:16,100
C'est bien ici la fête ?
Is this the party?

41
00:02:16,100 --> 00:03:05,850
C'est Valentin ?
Is it Valentin?

42
00:03:06,840 --> 00:03:08,400
Non, alors là, on n'en sait rien, Camille.
No, we have no idea, Camille.

43
00:03:09,120 --> 00:03:10,140
Ça peut être n'importe qui.
It could be anyone.

44
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,000
Il y a des gens très malintentieux.
There are people with very bad intentions out there.

45
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:11,500
Je suis consterné, tu sais.
I'm appalled, you know.

46
00:03:13,760 --> 00:03:14,360
Ok, c'est lui.
Ok, it's him.

47
00:03:15,190 --> 00:03:16,810
Je crois que je vais faire un AVC de honte.
I think I'm going to have a stroke from embarrassment.

48
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:18,520
Honte de quoi ?
Embarrassed about what?

49
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:20,020
C'est mon nom, là ?
Is that my name up there?

50
00:03:20,020 --> 00:03:20,600
Ah oui, c'est vrai.
Oh right, it is.

51
00:03:24,850 --> 00:03:25,330
Sérieux ?
Seriously?

52
00:03:26,220 --> 00:03:27,820
J'ai jamais vu ça, jamais !
I've never seen anything like it, never!

53
00:03:28,820 --> 00:03:29,880
Calme-toi, assieds-toi.
Calm down, sit down.

54
00:03:31,640 --> 00:03:32,740
Fais gaffe, tu réveilles bien au fond.
Careful, you're waking people up in the back.

55
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:36,860
Il se passe quoi ?
What's going on?

56
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,540
Écoute, j'en sais rien, je viens juste d'arriver.
Look, I have no idea, I just got here.

57
00:03:38,860 --> 00:03:40,600
Je crois que c'est à cause du tag qu'il y a en bas.
I think it's because of the tag downstairs.

58
00:03:41,220 --> 00:03:46,620
C'est immonde, voilà, c'est immonde.
It's disgusting, that's what it is, disgusting.

59
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:47,820
Ils charment très bien, là.
They're handling it quite well over there.

60
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:51,420
Mets-toi au mur, Camille.
Stand against the wall, Camille.

61
00:03:53,130 --> 00:03:55,130
On peut encore se faire fusiller avec dignité.
You can still face a firing squad with dignity.

62
00:03:58,760 --> 00:03:59,660
Camille Valentini, c'est moi.
Camille Valentini — that's me.

63
00:04:01,050 --> 00:04:02,690
Enfin, le fils de pute, quoi, c'est moi.
Well, the son of a bitch — that's me.

64
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:06,000
Parce qu'avec Camille, on a vécu quelque temps sous la même identité.
Because Camille and I lived under the same identity for a while.

65
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:09,320
On formait un agent à deux têtes, en quelque sorte, voilà.
We were a two-headed agent, in a way — that's how it was.

66
00:04:10,500 --> 00:04:12,480
Parce que je m'en sortais pas du tout toute seule.
Because I wasn't managing at all on my own.

67
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:16,000
Et du coup, ça permettait comme ça de doubler notre surface d'action.
And so it let us double our operational reach.

68
00:04:16,340 --> 00:04:18,900
Seulement, après, j'ai rencontré ce garçon un peu impulsif.
Only then I met this somewhat impulsive guy.

69
00:04:19,020 --> 00:04:20,000
J'ai vécu cette passion.
I lived through this passion.

70
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:20,920
Ah !
Ah!

71
00:04:21,490 --> 00:04:23,290
Il faut vraiment que vous la fermiez, tous les deux.
The two of you really need to shut up.

72
00:04:23,450 --> 00:04:24,490
Parce qu'on est en train de parler, là.
Because we're in the middle of a conversation here.

73
00:04:25,220 --> 00:04:26,300
Qu'est-ce que t'as ?
What's wrong with you?

74
00:04:27,220 --> 00:04:29,360
C'est une saloperie de traîne, voilà ce qu'il a.
It's a damn lag, that's what's wrong with him.

75
00:04:30,590 --> 00:04:33,250
En fait, j'aimerais bien qu'on arrête toute cette violence.
Actually, I'd really like us to stop all this violence.

76
00:04:33,570 --> 00:04:35,850
Parce que là, vraiment, ça commence à m'oppresser.
Because right now, honestly, it's starting to suffocate me.

77
00:04:35,870 --> 00:04:36,650
Cette violence ?
This violence?

78
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:38,410
Mais c'est pas toi qui m'as bouffé l'oreille, peut-être ?
Wasn't it you who bit my ear off, maybe?

79
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:39,390
Avec Tyson ?
Like Tyson?

80
00:04:39,730 --> 00:04:42,250
Vous êtes vraiment une belle bande d'hypocrites.
You're really a fine bunch of hypocrites.

81
00:04:42,670 --> 00:04:44,210
Personne ici n'a jamais supporté Hicham.
Nobody here ever liked Hicham.

82
00:04:44,850 --> 00:04:45,990
Osez me dire le contraire.
Go ahead and tell me otherwise.

83
00:04:46,610 --> 00:04:48,630
Toi, tu passais ton temps à dire qu'il était pas cultivé,
You spent all your time saying he wasn't cultured,

84
00:04:48,690 --> 00:04:49,750
qu'il avait pas sa place dans le métier.
that he had no place in this business.

85
00:04:49,990 --> 00:04:50,170
Non.
No.

86
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:52,390
Au début, j'ai vu qu'il avait quelques lacunes.
At first, I saw he had some gaps.

87
00:04:53,110 --> 00:04:54,110
Et après, j'ai changé.
And then I changed my mind.

88
00:04:54,530 --> 00:04:56,290
Et vous deux, vous étiez en train de monter votre propre agence
And the two of you were setting up your own agency

89
00:04:56,290 --> 00:04:56,950
dans le dos de tout le monde.
behind everyone's backs.

90
00:04:57,130 --> 00:04:57,250
Non.
No.

91
00:04:59,630 --> 00:05:00,870
C'était plus l'actualité, ça.
That was old news.

92
00:05:01,130 --> 00:05:03,190
C'est pas toi qui m'as dit que si Hicham partait, tu restais ?
Wasn't it you who told me that if Hicham left, you'd stay?

93
00:05:03,190 --> 00:05:03,770
Moi ?
Me?

94
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:05,690
Je suis en train d'essayer de sauver Aïska,
I'm trying to save Aïska,

95
00:05:05,850 --> 00:05:07,350
de faire qu'on retrouve un fonctionnement normal.
to get things back to running normally.

96
00:05:08,370 --> 00:05:09,510
Moralité, c'est moi qui suis le traître.
So morally, I'm the traitor.

97
00:05:09,690 --> 00:05:11,290
T'as dit moralité, là ?
Did you just say "morally"?

98
00:05:11,290 --> 00:05:13,170
Mathias, il faut pas employer des mots que tu comprends pas.
Mathias, you shouldn't use words you don't understand.

99
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:15,490
Euh, OK, ça suffit, je vais vous laisser entre vous.
Uh, OK, that's enough — I'll leave you to it.

100
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:16,770
Non, mais ça va, j'ai compris.
No, it's fine, I get it.

101
00:05:17,270 --> 00:05:18,550
Je suis pas le bienvenu ici, c'est ça ?
I'm not welcome here, is that it?

102
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:20,740
Félicitations, Mathias, t'as gagné.
Congratulations, Mathias, you win.

103
00:05:21,200 --> 00:05:22,640
Je te vends mes parts. Voilà.
I'll sell you my shares. There you go.

104
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:25,130
Maintenant, démerdez-vous pour trouver les 2 millions de dollars
Now, good luck finding the 2 million dollars

105
00:05:25,130 --> 00:05:25,870
pour de vos Américains.
for your Americans.

106
00:05:25,890 --> 00:05:26,670
Non, non, Hicham, attends.
No, no, Hicham, wait.

107
00:05:26,950 --> 00:05:28,310
Qu'est-ce que tu veux que j'attende ?
What do you want me to wait for?

108
00:05:28,310 --> 00:05:30,190
Quelqu'un ici a une meilleure proposition à me faire ?
Does anyone here have a better offer for me?

109
00:05:30,670 --> 00:05:31,770
Oui ? Non ?
Yes? No?

110
00:05:32,060 --> 00:05:34,140
Voilà, donc ce soir, on va fêter les 30 ans d'Aïska,
Right, so tonight we're celebrating Aïska's 30th anniversary,

111
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:36,700
et puis j'annoncerai le changement de direction.
and I'll announce the change in leadership.

112
00:05:36,800 --> 00:05:37,200
Ça va être super.
It'll be great.

113
00:05:38,690 --> 00:05:39,250
Joyeux anniversaire.
Happy anniversary.

114
00:05:42,270 --> 00:05:45,570
J'imagine que t'as une solution pour contrer les Américains, hein ?
I assume you have a plan to counter the Americans, right?

115
00:05:45,570 --> 00:05:47,390
Jamais tu prendrais le risque de leur devoir 2 millions.
You'd never risk owing them 2 million.

116
00:05:47,770 --> 00:05:48,810
Je sais ce que je fais, oui.
I know what I'm doing, yes.

117
00:05:49,190 --> 00:05:51,130
Il attend d'être le chef pour le sortir sans miracle.
He's waiting to be in charge before pulling it off like a miracle.

118
00:05:51,970 --> 00:05:54,550
Excusez-moi, mais en fait, y a la responsable de la fête de ce soir
Excuse me, but actually, the person running tonight's party

119
00:05:54,550 --> 00:05:55,250
qui vient juste d'arriver,
just arrived,

120
00:05:55,410 --> 00:05:57,290
et elle arrête pas de me bombarder de questions.
and she won't stop bombarding me with questions.

121
00:05:57,430 --> 00:05:58,830
J'ai envie de s'adresser à Mathias,
I'd like to address Mathias,

122
00:05:59,520 --> 00:06:00,720
puisque c'est lui le chef, maintenant.
since he's the one in charge now.

123
00:06:02,620 --> 00:06:02,980
Bonjour.
Hello.

124
00:06:03,740 --> 00:06:04,100
Bonjour.
Hello.

125
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:07,640
Oh, vous vous êtes fait mal ?
Oh, did you hurt yourself?

126
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:08,360
Oui, non, c'est pas grave.
Yes, no, it's nothing serious.

127
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:10,660
C'est dommage, le jour de la fête ?
What a shame, on the day of the party?

128
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:23,100
Alors, vous inquiétez pas, les néons vont arriver.
Don't worry, the neon lights are on their way.

129
00:06:23,820 --> 00:06:26,720
Et sinon, excusez-moi, on me parle en même temps.
And sorry, someone's talking to me at the same time.

130
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:27,940
Oui, Steph ?
Yes, Steph?

131
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:30,000
D'accord.
Alright.

132
00:06:30,440 --> 00:06:31,180
Très bien, merci.
Very good, thank you.

133
00:06:31,820 --> 00:06:35,020
Euh, y a un petit changement pour les compositions florales,
Uh, there's a small change for the floral arrangements,

134
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:36,680
mais voilà, ne vous inquiétez pas.
but don't worry about it.

135
00:06:37,700 --> 00:06:38,420
Et euh...
And uh...

136
00:06:38,600 --> 00:06:41,460
aussi, par rapport à l'agencement des différents espaces.
also, regarding the layout of the different spaces.

137
00:06:41,800 --> 00:06:44,140
On est bien d'accord qu'ici, à l'étage,
We're agreed that up here, on this floor,

138
00:06:44,180 --> 00:06:45,760
on est sur une ambiance tamisée,
we're going for a dimmed, relaxed atmosphere —

139
00:06:46,540 --> 00:06:47,740
lunch, chill-out...
lunch, chill-out...

140
00:06:47,740 --> 00:06:49,860
Vous faites très attention, là, avec ces verres, hein,
Be very careful with those glasses,

141
00:06:49,860 --> 00:06:50,640
ils sont super fragiles.
they're extremely fragile.

142
00:06:52,060 --> 00:06:53,600
Du coup, je me suis dit que sur le rooftop,
So I thought that on the rooftop,

143
00:06:53,740 --> 00:06:55,900
ce serait bien d'avoir quelque chose de quand même un peu plus festif,
it might be nice to have something a bit more festive,

144
00:06:56,380 --> 00:06:57,700
d'où l'idée du bar à cocktails,
hence the idea of a cocktail bar,

145
00:06:57,840 --> 00:07:00,720
avec des mojitos, des spritz, des cailloux.
with mojitos, spritzes, some rocks.

146
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,940
Non, non, mais attendez, c'est pas du tout ce qu'on avait convenu.
No, no, wait — that's not at all what we agreed on.

147
00:07:03,040 --> 00:07:04,880
On avait dit champagne uniquement.
We said champagne only.

148
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:06,180
On est bien d'accord ?
Are we clear on that?

149
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:06,920
Bien sûr.
Of course.

150
00:07:08,320 --> 00:07:09,840
Mathias, il faut que je vous parle une minute, s'il vous plaît.
Mathias, I need a word with you, please.

151
00:07:10,220 --> 00:07:12,700
Oui, Steph, est-ce que tu peux m'annuler le bar à cocktails, s'il te plaît ?
Yes, Steph, can you cancel the cocktail bar for me, please?

152
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:13,420
Merci.
Thank you.

153
00:07:19,300 --> 00:07:20,300
Mais Mathias, putain !
But Mathias, for God's sake!

154
00:07:20,560 --> 00:07:21,980
Mais il fallait me demander !
You should have asked me!

155
00:07:21,980 --> 00:07:24,540
Tout le monde le sait qu'une photocopieuse, c'est un historique !
Everyone knows a photocopier keeps a history!

156
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:26,820
Non, alors là, si c'est pour m'accabler, vous sortez tout de suite !
No, if you're just going to pile on, get out right now!

157
00:07:26,820 --> 00:07:27,860
Eh oh, vous baissez d'un ton, hein,
Hey, keep it down,

158
00:07:27,860 --> 00:07:29,680
parce que sinon, je vais vous mordre l'oreille, à vous aussi !
or I'll bite your ear off too!

159
00:07:31,760 --> 00:07:32,100
Excusez-moi.
Excuse me.

160
00:07:33,640 --> 00:07:34,660
Écoutez, ce qui est fait est fait.
Look, what's done is done.

161
00:07:35,280 --> 00:07:36,320
On a eu ce qu'on a voulu.
We got what we wanted.

162
00:07:36,640 --> 00:07:37,060
Hein ?
Hmm?

163
00:07:37,300 --> 00:07:38,060
Vous êtes le patron.
You're the boss.

164
00:07:38,720 --> 00:07:40,100
Alors maintenant, on se tourne vers l'avenir.
So now, we look ahead.

165
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:41,040
C'est ça, oui.
That's right, yes.

166
00:07:46,570 --> 00:07:48,930
Le Yi-King n'a jamais dit que ce serait facile, Mathias.
The I Ching never said it would be easy, Mathias.

167
00:07:49,470 --> 00:07:50,330
Vous avez percé.
You've broken through.

168
00:07:50,730 --> 00:07:51,770
La digue a cédé.
The dam has given way.

169
00:07:52,210 --> 00:07:53,050
Il y a de l'eau partout.
There's water everywhere.

170
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:55,050
Eh ben maintenant, on va éponger.
Well, now we mop it up.

171
00:07:55,290 --> 00:07:55,570
Voilà.
There we go.

172
00:07:56,150 --> 00:08:04,300
Non, non, je suis désolé.
No, no, I'm sorry.

173
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:07,180
Mais après ce qu'il a fait, je peux pas rester.
But after what he did, I can't stay.

174
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:07,660
C'est pas possible.
It's just not possible.

175
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:09,060
Non.
No.

176
00:08:09,840 --> 00:08:10,620
Tiens, vas-y, passe.
Here, go ahead, through you go.

177
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:13,040
Quitte à vivre la fin du monde, autant être stone.
If the world's ending anyway, might as well be stoned.

178
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:14,940
De toute façon, c'est ce que vous vouliez, non ?
Besides, it's what you wanted, isn't it?

179
00:08:15,360 --> 00:08:16,240
Alors allez-y, partez.
So go on then, leave.

180
00:08:16,680 --> 00:08:17,680
Arlette, on l'aurait pas fait.
Arlette, we never would have done it.

181
00:08:17,840 --> 00:08:18,560
C'était une phase.
It was a phase.

182
00:08:19,040 --> 00:08:19,320
Oui.
Yes.

183
00:08:20,580 --> 00:08:21,760
Allez, vas-y, fais tourner, là.
Come on, go ahead, run it.

184
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,240
Les chats, mais il les casse-couilles.
The cats, but he's a pain in the ass about them.

185
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:24,440
Mais où ?
But where?

186
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:24,960
Au moins, il est frontal.
At least he's upfront about it.

187
00:08:26,660 --> 00:08:26,940
Mathias.
Mathias.

188
00:08:28,480 --> 00:08:30,140
En 30 ans de métier, j'en ai vu des sales coups.
In 30 years in the business, I've seen some dirty moves.

189
00:08:30,220 --> 00:08:33,290
Mais alors là, montez là votre agence.
But this — go ahead and set up your agency.

190
00:08:33,430 --> 00:08:33,750
Je vous le dis.
I'm telling you.

191
00:08:34,830 --> 00:08:35,910
Il faut que je reprenne ma retraite.
I need to come out of retirement.

192
00:08:36,780 --> 00:08:38,780
Avec Guy, on a repéré une petite maison au Pays Basque.
Guy and I spotted a little house in the Basque Country.

193
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:39,420
Ah ben, tiens, voilà.
Ah, well, there you go.

194
00:08:39,580 --> 00:08:40,660
J'ai une bonne idée, ça, le Pays Basque.
That's a good idea, the Basque Country.

195
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:41,940
Moi aussi, je vais m'installer là-bas.
I'm going to move there too.

196
00:08:42,080 --> 00:08:43,040
Me mettre au surf, tiens.
Take up surfing, why not.

197
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:43,920
Ouais, ben ouais.
Yeah, well, yeah.

198
00:08:43,960 --> 00:08:46,120
Allez, venez tous en espadrille à bouffer de la pâte à négras.
Come on, everyone come in espadrilles and stuff yourselves on négra pastries.

199
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:46,980
Non, mais ça va pas, les gars.
No, seriously, are you out of your minds?

200
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:48,640
Oh ! On va pas laisser faire ça.
Oh! We're not going to let this happen.

201
00:08:49,590 --> 00:08:50,050
Oui ?
Yes?

202
00:08:50,370 --> 00:08:54,340
Est-ce que quelqu'un veut un petit thé ou un petit café ?
Would anyone like a little tea or coffee?

203
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:56,520
Je peux aussi aller chercher un petit smoothie, si vous préférez.
I can also grab a smoothie, if you'd prefer.

204
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:57,940
Non merci, ça va.
No thanks, we're fine.

205
00:08:58,420 --> 00:09:03,940
Mais je voudrais juste savoir si tout va bien.
I just want to know if everything's okay.

206
00:09:05,570 --> 00:09:08,210
Pour les deux Camille et Valentini, je veux dire, pas tout le reste.
For the two of you — Camille and Valentini — I mean, not all the rest of it.

207
00:09:08,230 --> 00:09:09,570
Ça, évidemment, je sais que ça va pas très bien.
That, obviously, I know isn't going great.

208
00:09:09,950 --> 00:09:12,430
Franchement, au point où on en est, on s'en fout total de tes conneries d'agents de double.
Honestly, at this point, we couldn't care less about your double-agent nonsense.

209
00:09:12,690 --> 00:09:13,090
D'accord.
Alright.

210
00:09:13,710 --> 00:09:13,990
Merci.
Thank you.

211
00:09:17,060 --> 00:09:18,000
Mais si on se tirait ?
What if we just left?

212
00:09:18,440 --> 00:09:19,600
Tu vois, on démissionne.
You know, we quit.

213
00:09:20,080 --> 00:09:21,240
C'est une forme de lutte aussi.
That's a form of resistance too.

214
00:09:21,700 --> 00:09:23,800
À la tronche de Mathias, s'il se retrouvait tout seul.
Just to see Mathias's face if he ended up all alone.

215
00:09:24,160 --> 00:09:24,840
Bien tout seul.
Completely alone.

216
00:09:28,990 --> 00:09:29,550
Hervé !
Hervé!

217
00:09:30,740 --> 00:09:33,180
Vous vous appeliez tous les deux Camille et Valentini, c'est bien ça ?
You're both called Camille and Valentini, is that right?

218
00:09:33,180 --> 00:09:33,620
Oui.
Yes.

219
00:09:34,100 --> 00:09:43,060
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

220
00:09:47,560 --> 00:09:48,160
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

221
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,240
Je sais que tout ça est très perturbant.
I know all of this is very unsettling.

222
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:51,420
Désolé.
I'm sorry.

223
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,160
Mais ça va rentrer dans l'ordre.
But things will sort themselves out.

224
00:09:53,810 --> 00:09:54,970
Je me sens tellement conne.
I feel like such an idiot.

225
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,880
Quoi, ton histoire d'agent double ? C'est rien, ça.
What, your double-agent thing? That's nothing.

226
00:09:58,140 --> 00:09:59,400
Ah oui, bah voilà, c'est ça, c'est rien.
Oh right, yeah, exactly, it's nothing.

227
00:10:00,750 --> 00:10:03,250
On flippait, mais à côté de vos combines, en fait, on est des amateurs.
We were panicking, but next to your schemes, we're actually amateurs.

228
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:07,100
Andrea, Gabriel, toi, c'est la trahison à tous les étages.
Andrea, Gabriel, you — it's betrayal at every level.

229
00:10:08,120 --> 00:10:08,920
Vous me dégoûtez.
You disgust me.

230
00:10:09,520 --> 00:10:13,720
Mais je crois que ce qui me fait le plus de peine, en fait, c'est que j'ai l'impression que t'adores ça.
But I think what hurts me most, actually, is that I get the feeling you love it.

231
00:10:23,320 --> 00:10:26,060
Le pouvoir de Mathias, là, maintenant, c'est qu'il peut résoudre le Huppergate.
Mathias's leverage right now is that he can resolve the Huppergate.

232
00:10:26,560 --> 00:10:29,240
Mais si on arrive à contrer les Américains avant lui, il a plus rien, il a plus de levier.
But if we manage to counter the Americans before he does, he's got nothing — no leverage left.

233
00:10:29,240 --> 00:10:32,420
Mais c'est trop tard. Il lui vend ses parts. Il annonce ce soir.
But it's too late. He's selling his shares. He's announcing tonight.

234
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:36,680
Écoute-moi, Isabelle Huppert a signé un contrat d'exclusivité avec les Américains.
Listen to me — Isabelle Huppert signed an exclusivity contract with the Americans.

235
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:39,840
Elle avait pas le droit de tourner dans un autre film et c'est pour ça qu'ils nous attaquent.
She wasn't allowed to shoot another film, and that's why they're suing us.

236
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,020
Oui, merci, mais ça, on sait.
Yes, thank you, but we know that.

237
00:10:41,380 --> 00:10:43,520
Et s'il y avait deux Isabelle Huppert ?
What if there were two Isabelle Hupperts?

238
00:10:44,910 --> 00:10:48,670
Elle a tourné dans le film de Cédric Kahn, ça, c'est un fait, on pourra pas le contester.
She shot Cédric Kahn's film — that's a fact, we can't contest it.

239
00:10:49,290 --> 00:10:52,190
Mais le litige, il porte sur une nuit seulement.
But the dispute only covers one night.

240
00:10:52,430 --> 00:10:54,510
La nuit où les deux tournages se sont chevauchés, donc.
The night the two shoots overlapped, specifically.

241
00:10:54,830 --> 00:10:59,890
Si cette nuit-là, c'était une autre Isabelle Huppert qui avait joué.
If that night, it was a different Isabelle Huppert who had played the role.

242
00:11:00,330 --> 00:11:00,690
C'est ça.
That's right.

243
00:11:00,710 --> 00:11:02,090
Mais je vois que t'as entamé le cerveau, ma pauvre.
But I can see your brain's gone soft, poor thing.

244
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:05,030
Non, une homonyme. Une meuf qui s'appelle vraiment Isabelle Huppert.
No, a namesake. A woman who's actually called Isabelle Huppert.

245
00:11:05,470 --> 00:11:06,550
Attends, ça doit bien exister, hein.
Come on, there must be one out there.

246
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:09,880
Excuse-moi, on t'a complètement perdu, quoi.
Excuse me, you've completely lost us here.

247
00:11:10,360 --> 00:11:11,980
Je sais pas, je suis sur la lumière, on va bien voir.
I don't know, I'm going with the light, let's see where it takes us.

248
00:11:15,440 --> 00:11:16,180
Il y en a deux.
There are two.

249
00:11:18,380 --> 00:11:22,100
Alors, il y en a une à Gentilly et l'autre à Épernay.
So, there's one in Gentilly and the other in Épernay.

250
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,140
C'est magnifique.
That's wonderful.

251
00:11:24,610 --> 00:11:25,510
Deux Isabelle Huppert.
Two Isabelle Hupperts.

252
00:11:27,100 --> 00:11:28,960
Bon, attends, admettons.
Alright, wait, let's say we go with that.

253
00:11:30,640 --> 00:11:33,880
Cédric Kahn a engagé un homonyme, OK ?
Cédric Kahn hired a namesake, OK?

254
00:11:34,380 --> 00:11:36,820
Donc, il va lui faire jouer le même rôle qu'Isabelle Huppert.
So he's going to have her play the same role as Isabelle Huppert.

255
00:11:36,940 --> 00:11:37,220
C'est ça.
That's right.

256
00:11:37,240 --> 00:11:40,820
Parce que là, sur la feuille, le rôle, c'est marqué en face du nom.
Because right there on the sheet, the role, it's written next to the name.

257
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:42,440
Marie de Médicis.
Marie de' Medici.

258
00:11:43,520 --> 00:11:44,100
Isabelle Huppert.
Isabelle Huppert.

259
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:48,520
Donc, dans ce film, Marie de Médicis sera jouée par deux femmes différentes
So in this film, Marie de' Medici will be played by two different women

260
00:11:49,180 --> 00:11:50,800
qui s'appelleront toutes les deux Isabelle Huppert.
who will both be called Isabelle Huppert.

261
00:11:51,890 --> 00:11:53,670
Putain, tu m'énerves, tu fais toujours de l'obstruction.
God, you drive me crazy, you're always being obstructive.

262
00:11:53,790 --> 00:11:57,050
Je crois que j'ai une idée.
I think I have an idea.

263
00:11:58,600 --> 00:12:00,840
Enfin, je suis pas sûre, mais je vais le dire quand même pour la discussion.
Well, I'm not sure, but I'll say it anyway, just for the discussion.

264
00:12:03,310 --> 00:12:06,010
C'était la nuit de la mort de Marie de Médicis, c'est bien ça ?
It was the night of Marie de' Medici's death, right?

265
00:12:06,010 --> 00:12:06,170
Oui.
Yes.

266
00:12:07,040 --> 00:12:08,820
La mort, c'est un dédoublement.
Death is a splitting in two.

267
00:12:09,540 --> 00:12:10,620
On devient quelqu'un d'autre.
You become someone else.

268
00:12:11,700 --> 00:12:12,340
Et ?
And?

269
00:12:12,740 --> 00:12:15,300
Donc, le homonyme aurait pu jouer Marie de Médicis, mais morte.
So the namesake could have played Marie de' Medici, but dead.

270
00:12:15,480 --> 00:12:17,220
Putain, son fantôme, c'est excellent !
Oh damn, her ghost — that's brilliant!

271
00:12:17,220 --> 00:12:18,060
Ça marche !
It works!

272
00:12:18,470 --> 00:12:18,860
Si !
It does!

273
00:12:19,260 --> 00:12:20,640
Arlette, ça marche !
Arlette, it works!

274
00:12:20,640 --> 00:12:23,860
Les Américains nous prennent déjà pour des branquilles non sous-développées.
The Americans already think we're underdeveloped crackpots.

275
00:12:23,980 --> 00:12:24,340
Ça passera pas.
This won't fly.

276
00:12:24,540 --> 00:12:26,720
Pourquoi pas ? Une femme qui s'appelle pareil pour jouer le fantôme,
Why not? A woman with the same name playing the ghost —

277
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,680
c'est beau, c'est poétique, c'est très cocteau !
it's beautiful, it's poetic, it's very Cocteau!

278
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,600
Ouais, c'est vrai.
Yeah, that's true.

279
00:12:30,200 --> 00:12:32,740
Et puis, comme on dit, plus c'est gros, plus ça passe.
And besides, as they say, the bigger the idea, the better it lands.

280
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:33,820
Oui, aussi.
True, too.

281
00:12:34,640 --> 00:12:35,320
Arlette a raison.
Arlette's right.

282
00:12:35,520 --> 00:12:36,120
Quand même.
Still.

283
00:12:37,770 --> 00:12:39,390
Pour que ça marche, il faut montrer des images.
For it to work, you need to show images.

284
00:12:39,890 --> 00:12:42,010
Donc il faut écrire une scène, il faut tourner des fourroches.
So we need to write a scene, we need to shoot some rushes.

285
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:43,960
Avant ce soir.
Before tonight.

286
00:12:44,930 --> 00:12:47,670
Tu préfères assister au sacre de Mathias devant tous nos talents ?
Do you prefer to watch Mathias be crowned in front of all our talent?

287
00:12:47,900 --> 00:12:51,840
Si je résume, on apporte le gâteau après le discours de M. Janowski.
So to summarize, we bring the cake after Mr. Janowski's speech.

288
00:12:52,460 --> 00:12:54,300
Et celui de M. Barneville.
And Mr. Barneville's.

289
00:12:54,900 --> 00:12:55,260
Évidemment.
Obviously.

290
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:58,400
Aux alentours de 23h, c'est bien ça ?
Around 11 PM, is that right?

291
00:12:58,430 --> 00:13:00,170
Parce qu'il faut que je sache à quelle heure le sortir du frigo.
Because I need to know what time to take it out of the fridge.

292
00:13:01,270 --> 00:13:04,190
Mathias ? 23h pour le gâteau, c'est bien, non ?
Mathias? 11 PM for the cake — that works, right?

293
00:13:04,190 --> 00:13:05,090
Oui, oui, c'est bien, oui.
Yes, yes, that's fine, yes.

294
00:13:06,010 --> 00:13:09,030
Sinon, j'ai pensé, voilà, pour finir en beauté,
Otherwise, I had a thought, just to end on a high note —

295
00:13:09,730 --> 00:13:10,870
pourquoi pas un petit lâcher ?
why not a little release?

296
00:13:10,890 --> 00:13:11,410
Un petit lâcher de ballons.
A little balloon release.

297
00:13:12,340 --> 00:13:12,980
De ballons ?
Balloons?

298
00:13:12,980 --> 00:13:13,280
Oui.
Yes.

299
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:15,020
Non, mais on va pas lâcher des ballons.
No, we're not releasing balloons.

300
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:16,040
C'est une fête professionnelle.
This is a professional event.

301
00:13:16,300 --> 00:13:17,860
Pourquoi pas un clown pendant qu'on y est ?
Why not throw in a clown while we're at it?

302
00:13:18,310 --> 00:13:19,390
Mais qu'est-ce qu'ils foutent, là ?
What the hell are they doing in there?

303
00:13:19,390 --> 00:13:21,270
Ça fait des heures qu'ils sont enfermés là-dedans.
They've been locked in there for hours.

304
00:13:21,710 --> 00:13:22,850
Écoutez, je repasse un peu plus tard.
Listen, I'll come back a little later.

305
00:13:23,430 --> 00:13:24,250
S'il vous plaît, oui.
Please, yes.

306
00:13:24,730 --> 00:13:35,270
Bon, j'appelle Hubert pour la prévenir.
Alright, I'll call Hubert to let her know.

307
00:13:35,330 --> 00:13:36,290
Non, arrête, surtout pas.
No, stop, whatever you do, don't.

308
00:13:36,730 --> 00:13:38,710
Mais non, c'est beaucoup trop risqué, puis ça va la stresser.
No, it's way too risky, and it'll just stress her out.

309
00:13:38,830 --> 00:13:39,710
Elle vient ce soir ?
Is she coming tonight?

310
00:13:39,710 --> 00:13:40,530
Non, elle est à Bilbao.
No, she's in Bilbao.

311
00:13:40,790 --> 00:13:41,550
Ben écoute, c'est pas plus mal.
Well, honestly, that's not the worst thing.

312
00:13:41,590 --> 00:13:43,390
On lui dira seulement si ça marche, d'accord ?
We'll only tell her if it works out, agreed?

313
00:13:43,390 --> 00:13:43,890
D'accord, t'as raison.
Agreed, you're right.

314
00:13:43,890 --> 00:13:45,990
OK, eh, tout le monde sait ce qu'il a à faire ?
OK, hey, does everyone know what they need to do?

315
00:13:45,990 --> 00:13:46,430
Oui.
Yes.

316
00:13:58,810 --> 00:13:59,510
Ça va ?
You good?

317
00:13:59,510 --> 00:14:00,970
Ben ouais, ça va super.
Yeah, totally fine.

318
00:14:01,390 --> 00:14:02,430
C'est la fête.
It's a party.

319
00:14:02,590 --> 00:14:04,330
Oui, oui, justement, c'est la fête.
Yes, yes, exactly, it's a party.

320
00:14:05,250 --> 00:14:07,850
Est-ce que ça fait trente ans que ça tient, avec ses hauts, avec ses bas ?
Has it held together for thirty years, through the highs and the lows?

321
00:14:07,850 --> 00:14:09,650
C'est grâce à nous, à nous quatre.
That's because of us, the four of us.

322
00:14:10,250 --> 00:14:12,170
On n'a pas besoin d'être amis pour faire tenir cette agence.
We don't need to be friends to keep this agency running.

323
00:14:12,390 --> 00:14:13,090
Dont agence ?
What agency?

324
00:14:13,090 --> 00:14:13,670
Notre agence.
Our agency.

325
00:14:14,590 --> 00:14:16,350
Je suis prêt à revaloriser vos parts.
I'm prepared to increase the value of your shares.

326
00:14:16,530 --> 00:14:17,150
À chacun.
For each of you.

327
00:14:18,150 --> 00:14:18,790
Ou vos fixes.
Or your salaries.

328
00:14:19,210 --> 00:14:21,410
Vos parts ou vos fixes, ou les deux, si vous voulez.
Your shares or your salaries, or both, if you want.

329
00:14:21,490 --> 00:14:22,330
Je suis prêt à discuter, voilà.
I'm open to talking, that's all.

330
00:14:22,530 --> 00:14:23,990
Mais on n'est pas les mendiants, Mathias, tu sais.
But we're not beggars, Mathias, you know that.

331
00:14:24,030 --> 00:14:24,290
Attends.
Hold on.

332
00:14:25,070 --> 00:14:25,870
Ça se réfléchit.
It's worth thinking about.

333
00:14:26,210 --> 00:14:26,650
Ben non.
No, it's not.

334
00:14:26,830 --> 00:14:27,990
Non, y a rien à réfléchir, non.
No, there's nothing to think about, no.

335
00:14:28,230 --> 00:14:29,370
Ah ben si, ça se réfléchit.
Oh yes there is, it's worth thinking about.

336
00:14:30,050 --> 00:14:32,250
Mais jamais oublier que les filles font des vertus apaisantes.
But never forget that women have a calming effect.

337
00:14:32,690 --> 00:14:37,560
Ben OK, ça se réfléchit.
OK fine, it's worth thinking about.

338
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:40,460
On va pas se déchirer ce soir devant tous nos talents, quand même.
We're not going to tear each other apart tonight in front of all our talent, come on.

339
00:14:40,660 --> 00:14:40,780
Non.
No.

340
00:14:41,080 --> 00:14:41,540
On vaut mieux que ça.
We're better than that.

341
00:14:41,740 --> 00:14:42,140
C'est vrai.
That's true.

342
00:14:42,640 --> 00:14:43,480
On vaut mieux que ça.
We're better than that.

343
00:14:53,300 --> 00:14:54,900
Fille de traître, c'est ça qu'il aurait dû écrire.
Traitor's daughter — that's what he should have written.

344
00:14:55,650 --> 00:14:56,310
Eh oh !
Hey!

345
00:14:56,310 --> 00:14:59,150
Pour accomplir de grandes choses, faut savoir se salir les mains un petit peu.
To accomplish great things, you have to be willing to get your hands a little dirty.

346
00:14:59,770 --> 00:15:00,970
Ah ben, j'hallucine.
I can't believe this.

347
00:15:01,570 --> 00:15:03,670
Toi, Mathias Luttre est quelqu'un, tu finirais par trouver ça sexy.
You, Mathias Luttre is somebody — you'd end up finding that sexy.

348
00:15:03,850 --> 00:15:05,970
Tu sais que tu deviens pathétique, en fait, à le défendre tout le temps, comme ça.
You know you're becoming pathetic, actually, always defending him like that.

349
00:15:06,410 --> 00:15:08,990
Et vous, vous étiez peut-être pas pathétique avec vos petites bidouilles.
And you — maybe you weren't so pathetic with your little schemes.

350
00:15:09,770 --> 00:15:12,070
On a tous un petit cadavre dans le placard, alors ça va, hein.
We've all got a skeleton in the closet, so let's leave it at that.

351
00:15:12,170 --> 00:15:12,830
Non, rien à voir.
No, not the same thing at all.

352
00:15:12,850 --> 00:15:13,930
Parce qu'en fait, nous, on a trahi personne.
Because the truth is, we never betrayed anyone.

353
00:15:14,190 --> 00:15:14,610
Ben si.
Yes you did.

354
00:15:14,730 --> 00:15:15,170
Moi ?
Me?

355
00:15:15,170 --> 00:15:16,570
Je croyais qu'on était amis.
I thought we were friends.

356
00:15:20,650 --> 00:15:21,850
Toi, tu dis rien, toi, hein.
You, keep your mouth shut, you hear me.

357
00:15:22,270 --> 00:15:22,910
Bien sûr.
Of course.

358
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:28,460
Ben, je crois qu'il y a plus rien à dire.
Well, I think there's nothing left to say.

359
00:15:31,440 --> 00:15:32,400
Allez-y, les filles.
Go ahead, ladies.

360
00:15:33,750 --> 00:15:34,990
C'est à moi de m'en occuper.
I'll handle this.

361
00:15:37,740 --> 00:15:38,480
Non, ben attends.
No, wait, hold on.

362
00:15:38,800 --> 00:15:39,500
On va t'aider.
We'll help you.

363
00:15:50,210 --> 00:15:50,930
Isabelle Huppert ?
Isabelle Huppert?

364
00:15:50,930 --> 00:15:51,210
Oui ?
Yes?

365
00:15:51,210 --> 00:15:54,570
Bonjour, Andréa Martel de l'agence INSCA, grande agence artistique.
Hello, Andréa Martel from the INSCA agency, a major talent agency.

366
00:15:54,730 --> 00:15:56,470
Voilà, c'est nous qui représentons Isabelle Huppert.
We're the ones who represent Isabelle Huppert.

367
00:15:56,470 --> 00:15:57,150
La vraie.
The real one.

368
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:58,090
Comment ça, la vraie ?
What do you mean, the real one?

369
00:15:58,630 --> 00:15:58,910
Merci.
Thank you.

370
00:15:59,130 --> 00:15:59,770
Non, pardon, pardon.
No, sorry, sorry.

371
00:15:59,910 --> 00:16:00,570
Je veux dire l'actrice.
I mean the actress.

372
00:16:00,770 --> 00:16:03,750
Mais aujourd'hui, en tout cas, c'est à vous que nous aimerions proposer un rôle.
But today, in any case, we'd like to offer a role to you.

373
00:16:04,090 --> 00:16:04,370
Ah.
Oh.

374
00:16:04,490 --> 00:16:05,070
Dans un film.
In a film.

375
00:16:05,210 --> 00:16:05,650
Ah non.
Oh no.

376
00:16:05,790 --> 00:16:06,230
Au cinéma.
In the cinema.

377
00:16:06,370 --> 00:16:07,430
Je vous arrête tout de suite.
Let me stop you right there.

378
00:16:07,530 --> 00:16:09,190
Le showbiz et les paillettes, c'est pas du tout mon truc.
Show business and the spotlight — that's really not my thing.

379
00:16:09,450 --> 00:16:09,730
Désolée.
Sorry.

380
00:16:09,930 --> 00:16:10,210
Attendez.
Wait.

381
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:11,010
Je vous ai même pas expliqué.
I haven't even explained yet.

382
00:16:11,090 --> 00:16:12,810
Non, mais parce que c'est vraiment pas grand-chose.
No, but it's really nothing major.

383
00:16:13,170 --> 00:16:15,670
On en a juste pour cet après-midi, puis ça peut être vraiment très amusant.
It's just for this afternoon, and it could actually be really fun.

384
00:16:15,790 --> 00:16:16,910
C'est pour aujourd'hui, en plus ?
It's for today, on top of everything?

385
00:16:16,910 --> 00:16:17,070
Oui.
Yes.

386
00:16:17,290 --> 00:16:18,630
Mais vous êtes marrantes, je travaille.
You're funny, I'm working.

387
00:16:18,710 --> 00:16:20,190
Moi, je suis de garde à l'hôpital.
I'm on call at the hospital.

388
00:16:39,690 --> 00:16:42,170
Quoi ? Je viens d'avoir Isabelle Huppert au téléphone.
What? I just had Isabelle Huppert on the phone.

389
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:44,680
C'est très important pour elle.
This is very important to her.

390
00:16:44,720 --> 00:16:45,260
Elle insiste.
She's insisting.

391
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:46,240
Ah bah oui.
Well, sure.

392
00:16:46,480 --> 00:16:48,920
Les patients qui m'attendent à l'hôpital, eux aussi, ils sont importants.
The patients waiting for me at the hospital — they're important too.

393
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,380
Vos patients, ils aiment bien le cinéma, non ?
Your patients, they like films, don't they?

394
00:16:51,380 --> 00:16:54,220
Est-ce que je peux vous avoir des photos dédicacées avec des places pour des avant-premières ?
Can I get you signed photos and tickets to premieres?

395
00:16:54,220 --> 00:16:54,680
Non, c'est gentil.
No, that's kind.

396
00:16:54,680 --> 00:16:56,160
Mais on a surtout besoin de moyens et de personnel.
But what we really need is funding and staff.

397
00:16:57,170 --> 00:16:58,690
Vous avez pas besoin d'entrer à l'Élysée, plutôt ?
Wouldn't you rather get into the Élysée for us?

398
00:16:58,690 --> 00:16:59,790
Ça, ça serait utile.
Now that would actually be useful.

399
00:17:00,810 --> 00:17:02,510
Et vous ? Vous voulez pas prendre soin de vous ?
And you? Don't you want to take care of yourself?

400
00:17:02,870 --> 00:17:06,390
Qu'est-ce que vous diriez de dormir dans une suite, dans un hôtel 5 étoiles avec un grand spa ?
How would you feel about sleeping in a suite at a 5-star hotel with a big spa?

401
00:17:06,390 --> 00:17:08,830
Déjà en claquettes et en peignons, j'en vois toute la journée. Non, merci.
I already see people in slippers and robes all day long. No, thank you.

402
00:17:09,370 --> 00:17:11,230
Et ce soir, il y a une grosse fête. Je vous invite.
And tonight there's a big party. I'm inviting you.

403
00:17:11,250 --> 00:17:14,150
C'est champagne, c'est cocktail, petit four par terre de stars.
Champagne, cocktails, canapés — wall-to-wall stars.

404
00:17:14,270 --> 00:17:15,770
Moi, je serais trop embarrassée.
I'd feel too out of place.

405
00:17:17,420 --> 00:17:20,660
Mais enfin, vous voulez pas sortir de votre zone de confort un petit peu ?
Come on, don't you want to step outside your comfort zone a little?

406
00:17:21,280 --> 00:17:24,680
Je vous propose quand même de prendre l'air, de quitter votre univers un peu glauque.
I'm offering you a chance to get some air, to leave your rather dreary world for a bit.

407
00:17:25,060 --> 00:17:26,340
Le temps d'une journée, c'est...
Just for a day, it's...

408
00:17:26,340 --> 00:17:28,260
C'est là que vous vous trompez. J'adore mon travail.
That's where you're wrong. I love my job.

409
00:17:28,640 --> 00:17:30,620
Et puis, pardon, parce que je vais louper le RER, là.
And excuse me, but I'm going to miss my train.

410
00:17:32,080 --> 00:17:33,600
Non, mais moi aussi, j'adore mon travail.
No, but I love my job too.

411
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:36,200
Mais mon agence, elle m'osait. Je suis dans la merde.
But my agency is crushing me. I'm in deep trouble.

412
00:17:36,580 --> 00:17:40,440
Je suis fatiguée.
I'm exhausted.

413
00:17:40,440 --> 00:17:41,820
Parce que mon bébé, il dort pas la nuit.
Because my baby doesn't sleep at night.

414
00:17:42,660 --> 00:17:44,420
Mais pour vous rattraper, j'ai couru vers l'autre.
And to catch you, I ran after the other one.

415
00:17:44,480 --> 00:17:45,680
Je me suis pissée dessus parce que j'ai...
I wet myself because I...

416
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:47,900
J'ai plus de périnée.
I have no pelvic floor left.

417
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:51,260
Oh là là, mais faut pas vous mettre dans des états pareils.
Oh goodness, you mustn't get yourself into such a state.

418
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:57,840
Vous venez d'avoir un bébé, c'est ça ?
You just had a baby, is that it?

419
00:17:58,340 --> 00:18:01,090
C'est normal, hein, de se sentir à cran, là.
It's normal to feel on edge, you know.

420
00:18:02,070 --> 00:18:05,680
Tenez, je vais vous donner une petite pastille à la menthe.
Here, let me give you a little mint.

421
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,240
Comme ça, ça va vous faire du bien, un peu de sucre.
There you go, a little sugar will do you good.

422
00:18:08,380 --> 00:18:08,940
Oui ?
Yes?

423
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:20,120
Bon, bah alors, racontez-moi. C'est quoi, votre affaire ?
Right then, tell me. What's going on with you?

424
00:18:26,340 --> 00:18:26,840
Yes ?
Yes?

425
00:18:26,840 --> 00:18:28,660
Charles, ça va ? Théo ?
Charles, you okay? Théo?

426
00:18:29,450 --> 00:18:30,450
À Londres ?
In London?

427
00:18:30,860 --> 00:18:32,800
J'ai pas beaucoup de temps, Andrea. Qu'est-ce que tu veux ?
I don't have much time, Andrea. What do you want?

428
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,660
Écoute, c'est à propos du dossier américain.
Look, it's about the American file.

429
00:18:34,700 --> 00:18:35,920
On a possiblement trouvé une solution.
We may have found a solution.

430
00:18:38,560 --> 00:18:40,180
Ça me regarde plus. Salut.
That's not my problem anymore. Bye.

431
00:18:40,560 --> 00:18:41,560
Mais si, ça te regarde.
Yes it is your problem.

432
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,600
Parce que si ça marche, ça veut dire qu'on aurait plus rien à payer.
Because if it works, it means we wouldn't owe anything anymore.

433
00:18:44,300 --> 00:18:45,940
Et donc, du coup, tu pourrais rester avec nous.
And so you could stay with us.

434
00:18:46,660 --> 00:18:47,980
T'en penses quoi ?
What do you think?

435
00:18:47,980 --> 00:18:49,420
Bon, tu m'écoutes, là ?
Hello, are you even listening?

436
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:49,640
Ouais.
Yeah.

437
00:18:50,640 --> 00:18:52,520
Hicham, je serai jamais partie. Pas après toi.
Hicham, I was never going to leave. Not after you.

438
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:53,280
Faut que tu me crois.
You have to believe me.

439
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:55,770
Faut que tu me croies et faut que tu restes.
You have to believe me and you have to stay.

440
00:18:56,170 --> 00:18:56,850
Attends, je dois te laisser.
Wait, I have to go.

441
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:59,020
Mais non, attends, putain !
No, wait, damn it!

442
00:19:08,490 --> 00:19:10,110
Mais qu'est-ce que c'est que ça ?
What on earth is that?

443
00:19:10,240 --> 00:19:11,780
J'ai dit fantôme, j'ai pas dit geisha.
I said ghost, not geisha.

444
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,680
J'ai que du talc. Je fais ce que je peux.
All I have is talcum powder. I'm doing my best.

445
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:17,120
Pardon, mais de toute façon, la lividité cadavérique, c'est pas blanc.
Sorry, but for the record, lividity isn't white.

446
00:19:17,420 --> 00:19:19,900
Si la personne vient juste de décéder, c'est plutôt rose bleutée.
If the person just died, it's more of a bluish pink.

447
00:19:20,620 --> 00:19:22,220
Non, je dis ça, mais je dis rien.
Not that I'm saying anything.

448
00:19:22,320 --> 00:19:23,660
Vous vous en foutez, au cinéma ?
You don't care about accuracy in films?

449
00:19:23,660 --> 00:19:25,180
Je fais quoi ? Je la dé-talque ?
What do I do? De-talc her?

450
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:26,080
Oui, s'il te plaît, oui.
Yes, please, yes.

451
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:33,080
Tu pouvais pas venir ce week-end ? Je me suis dit, allez hop, c'est moi qui y vais.
You couldn't come this weekend? I thought, right, I'll go to you.

452
00:19:34,390 --> 00:19:35,470
Juste pour la journée, comme ça.
Just for the day, that's all.

453
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,800
T'en veux pas ? T'es sûre ?
You don't want any? You sure?

454
00:19:39,800 --> 00:19:40,460
Non, ça va.
No, I'm fine.

455
00:19:41,590 --> 00:19:42,850
Je vais pas ramener tout ça à Rouda.
I can't bring all this back to Rouda.

456
00:19:43,430 --> 00:19:46,740
Elle va se vexer.
She'll take offence.

457
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:49,670
Quoi ?
What?

458
00:19:51,380 --> 00:19:52,500
Elle mange tôt, c'est ça ?
She eats early, is that it?

459
00:19:54,730 --> 00:19:55,050
Allez.
Come on.

460
00:20:02,040 --> 00:20:02,560
Arrête, papa.
Stop it, Dad.

461
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:04,620
C'est plutôt simple.
It's fairly straightforward.

462
00:20:30,470 --> 00:20:33,440
Non. Non, non, non, non.
No. No, no, no, no.

463
00:20:33,500 --> 00:20:35,200
Ça marchera jamais, votre histoire d'homonyme.
This lookalike scheme of yours will never work.

464
00:20:36,190 --> 00:20:39,510
En tant que productrice respectable et respectée,
As a respectable and respected producer,

465
00:20:40,040 --> 00:20:41,680
je ne peux pas cautionner un truc pareil.
I cannot endorse something like that.

466
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:43,040
Tu penses à l'envers, Laurence.
You're thinking about it backwards, Laurence.

467
00:20:43,440 --> 00:20:45,200
C'est si tu cautionnes pas que ça peut pas marcher.
It's if you don't endorse it that it can't work.

468
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:48,400
Arlette, je la connais pas, cette dame. Elle a jamais travaillé pour nous.
Arlette, I don't know this woman. She never worked for us.

469
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:49,840
J'ai pas lu signer un faux contrat de travail.
I didn't sign a fake employment contract.

470
00:20:51,530 --> 00:20:52,710
Je tremble pas là-dedans, moi.
I'm not getting mixed up in that.

471
00:20:55,900 --> 00:20:57,800
À moins que...
Unless...

472
00:20:57,800 --> 00:20:58,700
C'est ce que tu veux ?
Is that what you want?

473
00:21:00,140 --> 00:21:00,840
Vas-y, balance.
Go on, spit it out.

474
00:21:01,890 --> 00:21:05,730
On est en égo avec Guillaume Canet pour le film de Nicole Garcia ?
Are we in talks with Guillaume Canet for the Nicole Garcia film?

475
00:21:05,730 --> 00:21:07,190
Non, pas possible.
No, not possible.

476
00:21:08,040 --> 00:21:08,860
Je peux rien faire.
There's nothing I can do.

477
00:21:09,710 --> 00:21:10,710
Il est chez Barneville.
He's with Barneville.

478
00:21:11,150 --> 00:21:13,750
Mais si tu veux Guy Marchand pour le rôle du père, je te le fais pas cher.
But if you want Guy Marchand for the father's role, I can give you a good deal.

479
00:21:14,730 --> 00:21:16,490
Arlette, on l'a déjà, le père.
Arlette, we already have the father.

480
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:21,160
Par contre, Cécile de France, dans l'institutrice...
On the other hand, Cécile de France for the schoolteacher role...

481
00:21:21,160 --> 00:21:24,410
Ah ! Là, on parle.
Ah! Now we're talking.

482
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:28,080
Un accord de principe pour lancer le financement du film.
A deal in principle to greenlight the film's financing.

483
00:21:28,260 --> 00:21:28,920
OK, super.
OK, great.

484
00:21:29,460 --> 00:21:31,970
On est d'accord ?
Are we agreed?

485
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:34,420
Disons que c'est un bon début.
Let's say it's a good start.

486
00:21:34,800 --> 00:21:35,740
Quoi encore ?
What now?

487
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:39,120
Balasco, en participation exceptionnelle.
Balasco, in a special appearance.

488
00:21:40,770 --> 00:21:42,230
Tu t'es fait chier, Laurence.
You went all out, Laurence.

489
00:21:44,900 --> 00:21:45,580
Allez, signe.
Come on, sign it.

490
00:21:54,570 --> 00:21:54,930
Salut.
Hey.

491
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:56,090
Salut.
Hey.

492
00:21:58,770 --> 00:22:01,370
Excuse-moi, je voulais te parler d'un truc de boulot.
Sorry, I wanted to talk to you about a work thing.

493
00:22:02,480 --> 00:22:04,980
C'est... Ça, ça concerne la SKA, en fait.
It's... it's actually about SKA.

494
00:22:06,920 --> 00:22:07,980
Tu déménages ?
Are you moving?

495
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:09,020
Ah, je t'ai pas dit ?
Oh, I didn't tell you?

496
00:22:09,570 --> 00:22:11,410
Je pars à Los Angeles, tourner avec Ryan Gosling.
I'm off to Los Angeles to shoot with Ryan Gosling.

497
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:16,080
Non. Je retourne à Vitry-sur-Seine, habiter chez mes parents.
No. I'm moving back to Vitry-sur-Seine, to my parents'.

498
00:22:17,960 --> 00:22:20,040
T'aurais dû m'en parler, j'aurais peut-être pu t'aider, je sais pas.
You should've told me, maybe I could've helped somehow, I don't know.

499
00:22:20,360 --> 00:22:21,820
Ben non, parce que quand tu m'aides, ça m'aide pas, en fait.
Well no, because when you help me, it doesn't actually help.

500
00:22:23,450 --> 00:22:26,210
Bon, écoute, Sophia, moi, j'y suis pour rien si le film de Julien a pas marché, d'accord ?
Look, Sophia, it's not my fault Julien's film didn't work out, OK?

501
00:22:26,210 --> 00:22:27,250
Ben, t'aurais dû me dire de pas le faire.
You should've told me not to do it.

502
00:22:29,990 --> 00:22:30,530
Je te l'ai dit.
I did tell you.

503
00:22:31,470 --> 00:22:32,690
Mais j'ai pas arrêté de te le dire.
I told you over and over.

504
00:22:32,970 --> 00:22:34,170
Oui, mais tu pensais à toi, pas à moi.
Yeah, but you were thinking about yourself, not me.

505
00:22:34,970 --> 00:22:36,990
Moi, depuis, ça fait six mois que j'ai pas bossé,
Meanwhile, I haven't worked in six months,

506
00:22:37,010 --> 00:22:38,170
que je gagne pas un rond,
I'm not making a penny,

507
00:22:38,650 --> 00:22:40,170
et que tout ce qu'on me propose, c'est de me foutre à boile.
and every offer I get is to go do some crap online.

508
00:22:40,530 --> 00:22:41,790
Alors que toi, ça va, la vie ?
But apart from that, life's good for you, is it?

509
00:22:41,790 --> 00:22:42,710
Ah ouais, moi, ça va, la vie, ouais.
Oh yeah, life's great for me, sure.

510
00:22:42,970 --> 00:22:43,990
Évidemment, moi, ça va, la vie, ouais.
Obviously, life's great for me, sure.

511
00:22:44,450 --> 00:22:45,830
J'ai perdu la meuf que j'aimais le plus au monde.
I lost the woman I loved most in the world.

512
00:22:45,830 --> 00:22:48,870
J'ai perdu ma dignité en me comportant comme le dernier des abrutis.
I lost my dignity by acting like a complete idiot.

513
00:22:48,990 --> 00:22:50,450
Je vais peut-être perdre mon agence aussi, tiens, ce soir.
And I might lose my agency tonight too, as it happens.

514
00:22:51,110 --> 00:22:52,130
Mais à part ça, ça va, la vie.
But other than that, life's great.

515
00:22:53,410 --> 00:22:54,850
OK, excuse-moi de t'avoir dérangé, hein.
OK, sorry to have bothered you.

516
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:56,630
Bonne soirée.
Have a good evening.

517
00:23:03,610 --> 00:23:04,170
Gabriel ?
Gabriel?

518
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:08,450
Qu'est-ce qui se passe chez SK ?
What's going on at SK?

519
00:23:23,820 --> 00:23:24,660
Voilà, vous m'êtes là.
Great, you're all here.

520
00:23:25,040 --> 00:23:25,980
C'est super, la robe.
The dress is stunning.

521
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,020
Je finis avec la technique.
Let me finish with the technical side.

522
00:23:28,020 --> 00:23:30,540
La lumière, donc il me faut une lumière assez sophistiquée,
The lighting — I need something quite sophisticated,

523
00:23:30,640 --> 00:23:32,040
assez élégante, tu vois,
quite elegant, you see,

524
00:23:32,120 --> 00:23:34,880
parce que c'est intime et en même temps, je veux que ce soit spectaculaire.
because it's intimate, but at the same time I want it to be spectacular.

525
00:23:35,300 --> 00:23:37,460
Ce qu'il faut qu'on sente, c'est la relation de domination
What we need to feel is the dynamic of domination,

526
00:23:37,460 --> 00:23:38,300
un peu basse.
kept somewhat low-key.

527
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:40,980
La relation perverse entre le fantôme de la reine et sa confidente.
The perverse relationship between the queen's ghost and her confidante.

528
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:42,220
D'accord ? Ça, c'est hyper important.
Understood? That's absolutely crucial.

529
00:23:42,760 --> 00:23:44,720
OK, ouais, mais on n'a qu'une heure et demie, là.
OK, sure, but we've only got an hour and a half here.

530
00:23:45,840 --> 00:23:48,240
Tu vas pas aller loin, toi, si tu renonces comme ça au premier obstacle.
You won't get very far if you give up at the first hurdle.

531
00:23:48,780 --> 00:23:50,400
Bon, allez, on va se mettre en place.
Right, let's get into position.

532
00:23:50,760 --> 00:23:52,360
Sofia, tu vas te mettre près de l'arbre, s'il te plaît.
