726
00:32:04,340 --> 00:32:06,240
Mais rien, vous leur dites bonsoir, c'est tout.
Nothing, just say good evening, that's all.

727
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:08,020
Et si on vous demande, vous vous appelez Corinne,
And if anyone asks, your name is Corinne,

728
00:32:08,020 --> 00:32:09,380
vous êtes comédienne de théâtre en Provence.
you're a stage actress from Provence.

729
00:32:09,740 --> 00:32:11,280
Mais surtout, pas un mot de notre affaire.
But above all, not a word about our business.

730
00:32:11,280 --> 00:32:11,820
Pas de personne.
Not to anyone.

731
00:32:12,360 --> 00:32:13,620
Andréa, on peut se parler ?
Andréa, can we talk?

732
00:32:13,620 --> 00:32:14,140
Non, pas maintenant.
No, not now.

733
00:32:14,280 --> 00:32:15,500
S'il te plaît, c'est important.
Please, it's important.

734
00:32:17,710 --> 00:32:19,370
Hervé, Hervé, tu peux venir, s'il te plaît ?
Hervé, Hervé, can you come here, please?

735
00:32:20,750 --> 00:32:23,470
Hervé, c'est Corinne, tu sais, mon amie dont je t'ai parlé.
Hervé, this is Corinne, you know, my friend I told you about.

736
00:32:23,930 --> 00:32:25,150
Oui, bien sûr, bonsoir.
Yes, of course, good evening.

737
00:32:25,410 --> 00:32:25,730
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

738
00:32:25,850 --> 00:32:27,570
Hervé, je te la confie ?
Hervé, will you look after her?

739
00:32:27,570 --> 00:32:28,410
Oui, oui, oui.
Yes, yes, of course.

740
00:32:31,760 --> 00:32:32,860
Je veux bien un peu de champagne.
I'd love some champagne.

741
00:32:33,600 --> 00:32:34,180
Bien sûr.
Of course.

742
00:32:38,040 --> 00:32:41,240
Qu'est-ce qui va se passer, alors ?
So what's going to happen?

743
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:43,880
Tu vas partir ? Vous allez tous partir ?
Are you leaving? Are you all going to leave?

744
00:32:43,880 --> 00:32:44,500
Non.
No.

745
00:32:45,660 --> 00:32:45,980
Non.
No.

746
00:32:46,620 --> 00:32:48,040
Genre, vous allez négocier avec Mathias ?
What, you're going to negotiate with Mathias?

747
00:32:48,750 --> 00:32:49,610
Je n'y crois pas une seconde.
I don't believe that for a second.

748
00:32:50,030 --> 00:32:51,290
Non, écoute, Camille, ça va se tasser.
No, listen, Camille, it'll blow over.

749
00:32:51,970 --> 00:32:53,670
Comment ça, ça va se tasser ? Dis-moi la vérité.
What do you mean, blow over? Tell me the truth.

750
00:32:53,950 --> 00:32:55,270
C'est de mon amie aussi, hein, qu'il s'agit.
She's my friend too, you know.

751
00:32:55,830 --> 00:32:57,790
Je vais faire quoi, moi ? Ça va devenir quoi, à Escar ?
What am I supposed to do? What's going to become of Escar?

752
00:32:59,280 --> 00:33:00,120
Ça va, Gérard ?
You okay, Gérard?

753
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:01,300
Ça va bien, merci, et vous ?
I'm fine, thanks, and you?

754
00:33:01,540 --> 00:33:02,820
Ça va très bien. Santé.
Very well. Cheers.

755
00:33:03,040 --> 00:33:05,080
Santé. C'est la première fois que je monte ici, c'est top, hein.
Cheers. This is my first time up here — it's great, isn't it.

756
00:33:05,160 --> 00:33:05,920
C'est le temps de le dire.
I'll say.

757
00:33:06,980 --> 00:33:07,580
Ouais, c'est beau.
Yeah, it's beautiful.

758
00:33:07,780 --> 00:33:08,400
À tout à l'heure.
See you later.

759
00:33:09,260 --> 00:33:09,720
À toute.
See you.

760
00:33:11,850 --> 00:33:12,950
Bon, allez, arrête de te prendre la tête.
Come on, stop stressing yourself out.

761
00:33:13,470 --> 00:33:17,880
Qu'est-ce qui se passe ?
What's going on?

762
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:20,160
Il ne veut pas fonctionner quand on le branche, ça fait un court circuit.
It won't work when we plug it in — it's short-circuiting.

763
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:23,370
Non, mais c'est insensé, il faut joindre le fabricant.
No, this is ridiculous, you need to contact the manufacturer.

764
00:33:24,440 --> 00:33:25,760
Il n'y a pas une hotline ?
Isn't there a hotline?

765
00:33:25,760 --> 00:33:26,860
Non, ils n'ont pas de hotline.
No, they don't have a hotline.

766
00:33:27,540 --> 00:33:30,000
Excusez-moi, mesdames, je vais vous l'emprunter deux secondes.
Excuse me, ladies, I'm going to borrow him for two seconds.

767
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:32,300
Oui, je vous en prie, monsieur Lambin, avec joie.
Of course, Mr. Lambin, with pleasure.

768
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:36,020
Bon, hé, et donc, le néon ?
So, hey — what about the neon?

769
00:33:36,770 --> 00:33:39,170
Ah, parce que vous avez vu les invités, là, le standing.
Well, have you seen the guests — the calibre of people here.

770
00:33:39,410 --> 00:33:41,190
Oui, je sais, écoutez, on fait de notre mieux.
Yes, I know, listen, we're doing our best.

771
00:33:41,940 --> 00:33:42,800
J'espère bien, oui.
I certainly hope so.

772
00:33:44,660 --> 00:33:46,740
Moi, il se passe quoi, chez Escar, là ?
What's going on at Escar anyway?

773
00:33:47,440 --> 00:33:48,500
Rien, pourquoi ?
Nothing, why?

774
00:33:48,500 --> 00:33:51,100
Non, parce que j'ai entendu ta fille, enfin, j'ai pas tout compris, hein,
No, because I overheard your daughter — I didn't catch everything, mind you,

775
00:33:51,120 --> 00:33:53,020
mais elle avait la raquette pour l'agence, c'est quoi l'histoire ?
but she seemed upset about the agency — what's the story?

776
00:33:55,210 --> 00:33:59,210
En fait, je vais reprendre les rênes d'Escar.
Actually, I'm going to take the reins at Escar.

777
00:33:59,990 --> 00:34:03,210
On va l'annoncer tout à l'heure, c'est pour ça qu'il y a un peu d'agitation dans l'air, tu comprends ?
We're announcing it later — that's why there's a bit of a buzz in the air, you understand?

778
00:34:03,210 --> 00:34:06,190
Tu restes toujours agent ?
Are you staying on as an agent?

779
00:34:06,190 --> 00:34:06,590
Bien évidemment.
Absolutely.

780
00:34:07,150 --> 00:34:07,650
Ah, ouais ?
Oh yeah?

781
00:34:07,650 --> 00:34:10,620
Je te demande d'être discret.
I'm asking you to be discreet.

782
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:11,380
Bien sûr.
Of course.

783
00:34:12,380 --> 00:34:13,620
Quel embelli, dis-moi, un patron.
What a charmer, I have to say, a real boss.

784
00:34:15,200 --> 00:34:22,220
Hé, doucement, quand même.
Hey, easy now.

785
00:34:23,120 --> 00:34:26,680
Oh, ça fait des biens de se lâcher, sortir un peu de sa zone de confort, quoi.
Oh, it does you good to let loose, step outside your comfort zone a little.

786
00:34:27,020 --> 00:34:30,880
Un petit verre d'eau entre chaque verre d'alcool, c'est une technique très sous-estimée
A small glass of water between each alcoholic drink — it's a very underrated technique

787
00:34:30,880 --> 00:34:33,040
et ça évite de passer toute la nuit, là, t'es dans les toilettes.
and it keeps you from spending the whole night in the bathroom.

788
00:34:35,620 --> 00:34:36,950
Oh, il y a la rousse.
Oh, there's the redhead.

789
00:34:37,250 --> 00:34:37,990
Audrey Fleureau, oui.
Audrey Fleureau, yes.

790
00:34:38,030 --> 00:34:38,950
Et on montre pas du doigt.
And we don't point.

791
00:34:40,510 --> 00:34:42,790
Audrey Fleureau, bonsoir.
Audrey Fleureau, good evening.

792
00:34:43,110 --> 00:34:43,550
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

793
00:34:43,890 --> 00:34:50,630
On dit que les actrices, elles payent pas de mine quand on les voit en vrai, mais vous, très belles.
They say actresses don't look like much in person, but you — very beautiful.

794
00:34:50,950 --> 00:34:51,690
Merci beaucoup.
Thank you very much.

795
00:34:52,050 --> 00:34:52,450
C'est vrai.
It's true.

796
00:34:52,830 --> 00:34:54,410
Et vous êtes ?
And you are?

797
00:34:54,410 --> 00:34:55,370
Isabelle Huppert.
Isabelle Huppert.

798
00:34:55,750 --> 00:34:56,410
Très drôle.
Very funny.

799
00:34:56,810 --> 00:34:57,470
Corine !
Corine!

800
00:34:57,470 --> 00:34:59,610
Elle fait de ses blagues, ce soir.
She's full of jokes tonight.

801
00:35:01,830 --> 00:35:03,110
Je vous aime beaucoup.
I love you very much.

802
00:35:03,550 --> 00:35:03,790
Merci.
Thank you.

803
00:35:04,030 --> 00:35:05,730
Même quand vous couchez avec des nazis.
Even when you sleep with Nazis.

804
00:35:06,350 --> 00:35:07,730
Dans un village français, vous êtes.
In a French village, you are.

805
00:35:07,850 --> 00:35:09,150
Oui, merci, Herbège, avec vous.
Yes, thank you, Herbège, with you.

806
00:35:10,110 --> 00:35:17,580
Pardon, je me suis toujours demandé si vos poissons, c'est des vrais.
Excuse me, I've always wondered if your fish are real.

807
00:35:17,680 --> 00:35:21,020
Ils sont extraordinaires.
They're extraordinary.

808
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:22,160
Ça revient tout de suite, Audrey.
Audrey will be right back.

809
00:35:26,100 --> 00:35:26,960
Ça va, Audrey ?
You okay, Audrey?

810
00:35:26,960 --> 00:35:28,460
Vous passez une bonne soirée ?
Are you having a good evening?

811
00:35:28,460 --> 00:35:32,360
Très bonne, parce que là, par exemple, je viens de rencontrer Isabelle Huppert en version complètement folle.
A great one, because just now, for instance, I met Isabelle Huppert — totally unhinged version.

812
00:35:33,520 --> 00:35:34,620
Isabelle Huppert ?
Isabelle Huppert?

813
00:35:34,620 --> 00:35:38,740
C'est pas coutu.
That's not it.

814
00:35:38,940 --> 00:35:40,000
Ah, mais c'est pas ça, non ?
Oh, but that's not it, is it?

815
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:41,020
Ah, c'est pas ça.
Ah, that's not it.

816
00:35:42,870 --> 00:35:44,800
Ah, pardon, monsieur.
Oh, sorry, sir.

817
00:35:44,840 --> 00:35:45,300
C'est pas ça, non ?
That's not it, is it?

818
00:35:45,300 --> 00:35:46,300
J'adore tes délices.
I love your delights.

819
00:35:47,700 --> 00:35:50,820
C'est dingue, ce que tu peux voir.
It's incredible, what you can see.

820
00:35:51,460 --> 00:35:54,920
Tu peux voir la baleine, tu peux voir l'iceberg, tu peux voir des geysers qui pèlent à 15 mètres.
You can see whales, you can see icebergs, you can see geysers exploding 15 meters away.

821
00:35:54,980 --> 00:35:56,940
Il fait froid, justement, c'est ça, le chaud froid qui fait.
It's cold, but that's exactly it — the hot and cold contrast is what does it.

822
00:35:57,800 --> 00:35:58,560
Ah, j'aime bien.
Oh, I like that.

823
00:35:58,600 --> 00:35:59,680
Toi, tu travailles dans une catégorie ?
And you, do you work in a particular field?

824
00:35:59,680 --> 00:36:01,740
Moi, je suis scénariste. J'écris des séries.
I'm a screenwriter. I write series.

825
00:36:02,340 --> 00:36:03,260
Des séries ? Ah, d'accord.
Series? Oh, right.

826
00:36:04,200 --> 00:36:06,940
Parce que moi, justement, j'ai un projet là-dessus sur une série.
Because actually, I happen to have a project — a series.

827
00:36:07,360 --> 00:36:07,820
Ah ?
Oh?

828
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:14,620
Ouais, sur un type qui, en fait, qui essaie d'apprendre à survivre dans la forêt.
Yeah, about a guy who's basically trying to learn how to survive in the forest.

829
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:17,450
Il est seul, il est des quoi de bons seuls.
He's alone, he's completely on his own.

830
00:36:17,670 --> 00:36:18,910
Je sais pas, pour l'instant, le déserteur.
I don't know yet — for now, the working title is "The Deserter."

831
00:36:19,130 --> 00:36:20,370
Je pense qu'il y a un gros potentiel.
I think there's huge potential.

832
00:36:20,370 --> 00:36:22,510
Je pense qu'il y a un moyen, en fait, de développer vraiment le...
I think there's actually a way to really develop the...

833
00:36:23,310 --> 00:36:24,930
De développer ça en série.
To develop it into a series.

834
00:36:25,070 --> 00:36:25,710
Ça pourrait...
It could...

835
00:36:25,710 --> 00:36:26,810
On va aller prendre l'air sur la terrasse.
Let's go get some air on the terrace.

836
00:36:27,670 --> 00:36:29,770
Et donc, le gars est tout seul, quoi.
So the guy is completely alone.

837
00:36:29,910 --> 00:36:30,590
Oui, il est tout seul.
Yes, he's all alone.

838
00:36:31,190 --> 00:36:34,370
C'est ce qu'on est seul quand on est avec des arbres, tu vois.
It's that kind of lonely you feel when you're surrounded by trees, you know.

839
00:36:34,830 --> 00:36:38,080
À l'époque, plus personne ne se souvient de rien.
Back then, no one remembers anything anymore.

840
00:36:38,720 --> 00:36:39,960
Tiens, Martine Carole.
Oh look, Martine Carole.

841
00:36:40,040 --> 00:36:41,700
Vous connaissez Martine Carole ?
Do you know Martine Carole?

842
00:36:43,690 --> 00:36:44,410
Lola Montes.
Lola Montes.

843
00:36:45,730 --> 00:36:46,450
Caroline Chéry.
Caroline Chérie.

844
00:36:46,610 --> 00:36:50,210
Mais celle qui était avant Bardot, c'est Bardot qui l'a détruite.
But she was before Bardot — Bardot destroyed her.

845
00:36:50,450 --> 00:36:51,190
C'est Bardot, je connais.
I know Bardot.

846
00:36:51,350 --> 00:36:52,430
Ben, heureusement que vous connaissez.
Well, good thing you know someone.

847
00:36:52,450 --> 00:36:53,070
Je connais, c'est Bardot.
I know her, it's Bardot.

848
00:36:54,080 --> 00:36:57,720
Mais vous êtes agent, et vous savez pas qui est Martine Carole ?
But you're an agent and you don't know who Martine Carole is?

849
00:36:57,720 --> 00:36:59,660
Non, mais vraiment.
No, I really don't.

850
00:36:59,940 --> 00:37:01,480
C'est super, c'est...
That's amazing, it's...

851
00:37:01,480 --> 00:37:03,920
Et en plus, je vais tourner dans le prochain film d'Agnès Jamy.
And on top of that, I'm shooting Agnès Jamy's next film.

852
00:37:04,400 --> 00:37:06,260
C'est magnifique, bravo.
That's wonderful, congratulations.

853
00:37:06,620 --> 00:37:06,960
Merci.
Thank you.

854
00:37:08,620 --> 00:37:10,460
Et toi, tu fais quoi, en ce moment ?
And you, what are you up to these days?

855
00:37:10,460 --> 00:37:12,340
Moi, je fais plein de trucs, en fait.
Me, I've got a lot going on, actually.

856
00:37:12,560 --> 00:37:14,600
Tu sais, j'ai joué dans le film de Julien Doré.
You know, I was in Julien Doré's film.

857
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:20,000
Non, mais, enfin, c'est cool, quoi, parce que ça fait bouger pas mal de trucs, tu vois.
No, but, I mean, it's cool because it really gets things moving, you know.

858
00:37:20,180 --> 00:37:21,140
Ah, mais super !
Oh, that's great!

859
00:37:21,140 --> 00:37:22,500
Ouais, c'est vraiment super.
Yeah, it really is.

860
00:37:23,260 --> 00:37:25,020
Attends, mais c'est pas Olivier Assayès, là-bas ?
Wait, isn't that Olivier Assayas over there?

861
00:37:25,100 --> 00:37:27,120
J'adore ce mec.
I love that guy.

862
00:37:28,190 --> 00:37:30,110
Tu m'excuses, je reviens, hein ?
Excuse me, I'll be right back, okay?

863
00:37:30,110 --> 00:37:30,770
Ouais, ouais.
Yeah, yeah.

864
00:37:31,010 --> 00:37:53,020
On prend tout à zéro.
Back to square one.

865
00:37:53,460 --> 00:38:06,910
Bon, vous savez quoi, on va aller se reposer un peu dans un bureau.
Right, you know what, let's go get some rest in an office.

866
00:38:10,680 --> 00:38:11,960
Je les adore, elles.
I just love them.

867
00:38:13,260 --> 00:38:14,260
Oh, vous !
Oh, you!

868
00:38:15,250 --> 00:38:16,270
Je vous ai vues.
I've seen you before.

869
00:38:16,890 --> 00:38:18,840
Vous étiez dans quoi, déjà ?
What were you in again?

870
00:38:18,840 --> 00:38:21,060
Ah, c'est sûr que je vous ai vues.
I'm sure I've seen you somewhere.

871
00:38:21,340 --> 00:38:23,340
Oh, je sais plus du tout dans quoi...
Oh, I can't remember what it was at all...

872
00:38:23,900 --> 00:38:25,560
François Zapport, on joue avec les plus grands.
François Zapport — we work with the best.

873
00:38:26,060 --> 00:38:27,040
Et vous ?
And you?

874
00:38:27,860 --> 00:38:30,200
Bravo, mais quelle carrière !
Congratulations, what a career!

875
00:38:30,200 --> 00:38:31,340
Merci, merci.
Thank you, thank you.

876
00:38:31,720 --> 00:38:32,820
C'est très gentil.
That's very kind.

877
00:38:32,880 --> 00:38:33,880
Ça me touche beaucoup.
It means a lot to me.

878
00:38:34,750 --> 00:38:38,250
Tata Yo-Yo, mon fils, il a adoré cette chanson quand il était petit.
Tata Yo-Yo — my son absolutely loved that song when he was little.

879
00:38:39,290 --> 00:38:40,900
C'est pas moi, ça.
That's not me.

880
00:38:41,060 --> 00:38:42,000
C'est Annie Cordy.
That's Annie Cordy.

881
00:38:42,720 --> 00:38:43,500
Pardonnez-nous, mesdames.
Our apologies, ladies.

882
00:38:43,840 --> 00:38:45,700
Ah oui, c'était mon truc en plume.
Oh right, that was my feather boa number.

883
00:38:46,500 --> 00:38:46,940
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

884
00:38:47,900 --> 00:38:48,340
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

885
00:38:48,340 --> 00:38:49,380
On se connaît ?
Do we know each other?

886
00:38:49,380 --> 00:38:50,450
Je sais pas.
I'm not sure.

887
00:38:50,690 --> 00:38:52,010
Vous êtes connues ?
Are you famous?

888
00:38:52,570 --> 00:38:54,410
De quoi vous ne vous connaissez pas ?
How do you not know each other?

889
00:38:54,410 --> 00:38:55,350
C'est une amie comédienne.
She's a fellow actress.

890
00:38:56,330 --> 00:38:57,070
Isabelle Huppert.
Isabelle Huppert.

891
00:38:57,450 --> 00:38:59,590
Oh, ben comment vous le savez ?
Oh, how did you know that?

892
00:39:02,500 --> 00:39:02,960
Au revoir.
Goodbye.

893
00:39:07,900 --> 00:39:08,340
Rentrez.
Head inside.

894
00:39:10,110 --> 00:39:13,610
Catherine, tu t'emmènes ?
Catherine, are you leaving?

895
00:39:15,700 --> 00:39:18,200
Euh, mais tu veux pas que...
Um, but don't you want...

896
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:20,370
On s'entend pas, là.
I can't hear a thing in here.

897
00:39:20,370 --> 00:39:21,390
Tu veux pas aller dans mon bureau ?
Don't you want to go to my office?

898
00:39:21,390 --> 00:39:28,560
Non, je suis pas à l'aise ici, Mathias.
No, I'm not comfortable here, Mathias.

899
00:39:28,740 --> 00:39:40,450
Mon voyage en Inde, j'arrive plus à faire semblant.
Since my trip to India, I can't keep pretending.

900
00:39:40,770 --> 00:39:46,860
Qu'on va y arriver, que ça va aller, que...
That we'll figure it out, that everything will be fine, that...

901
00:39:51,310 --> 00:39:53,030
C'est un essai de se dire la vérité pour une fois.
This is an attempt to tell each other the truth for once.

902
00:40:05,020 --> 00:40:05,880
Il y a quelqu'un d'autre.
There's someone else.

903
00:40:06,240 --> 00:40:18,660
C'est toi qui viens de...
You're the one who just...

904
00:40:19,680 --> 00:40:21,880
Ben oui, je viens de te dire que j'ai rencontré quelqu'un.
Yeah, I just told you I met someone.

905
00:40:25,810 --> 00:40:26,290
Toi aussi.
You too.

906
