1095
00:50:17,120 --> 00:50:18,220
C'est aussi nos bébés.
They're our babies too.

1096
00:50:18,600 --> 00:50:20,480
Mais pour nous, c'est très important.
But for us, it matters a great deal.

1097
00:50:21,160 --> 00:50:22,920
Bien sûr, mais alors sans Laurence...
Of course, but then without Laurence...

1098
00:50:22,920 --> 00:50:23,820
Ah, c'est parti tout seul.
Oh, it just happened on its own.

1099
00:50:23,920 --> 00:50:25,500
Ah, Laurence, c'est parti tout seul.
Oh, Laurence, it just happened on its own.

1100
00:50:25,540 --> 00:50:27,020
Ça veut dire qu'il faut le lâcher, le bébé.
Which means you have to let go of the baby.

1101
00:50:27,520 --> 00:50:28,660
Allez, on accouche.
Come on, let's give birth.

1102
00:50:49,080 --> 00:50:53,820
Je reviens du royaume des morts.
I'm back from the land of the dead.

1103
00:50:55,340 --> 00:50:57,280
C'est vraiment votre film.
This is truly your film.

1104
00:50:59,400 --> 00:51:00,660
C'est un premier montage.
It's a first cut.

1105
00:51:01,740 --> 00:51:02,980
Work in progress.
Work in progress.

1106
00:51:03,360 --> 00:51:06,300
Et Isabelle Huppert est OK avec ça.
And Isabelle Huppert is OK with that.

1107
00:51:06,800 --> 00:51:09,020
Je cours. Je cours, je l'adore.
I'm running. I'm running, I adore her.

1108
00:51:09,320 --> 00:51:09,780
C'est bien.
That's good.

1109
00:51:09,900 --> 00:51:13,330
C'est quoi ça ?
What's that?

1110
00:51:14,400 --> 00:51:15,180
La chaussure.
The shoe.

1111
00:51:15,860 --> 00:51:17,360
Ça aussi, c'est sur la liste ?
That's on the list too?

1112
00:51:17,360 --> 00:51:18,560
Ah non, mais ça, c'est de ma faute.
Oh no, that one's my fault.

1113
00:51:18,840 --> 00:51:20,260
Je peux pas mettre d'autres chaussures.
I can't wear any other shoes.

1114
00:51:20,420 --> 00:51:22,100
C'est mon petit caprice de star à moi, quoi.
It's my little star moment, you know.

1115
00:51:22,580 --> 00:51:23,660
Parce que j'ai un...
Because I have a...

1116
00:51:24,280 --> 00:51:25,360
Un anus valgus.
A valgus anus.

1117
00:51:26,100 --> 00:51:27,240
Un anus ?
A what?

1118
00:51:28,840 --> 00:51:30,140
Non, un anus valgus.
No, a valgus — it's a foot thing.

1119
00:51:30,540 --> 00:51:32,860
C'est quand on a deux orteils qui se chevauchent comme ça.
It's when two toes overlap like this.

1120
00:51:33,020 --> 00:51:34,500
Et comme je suis debout toute la journée
And since I'm on my feet all day

1121
00:51:35,040 --> 00:51:37,960
avec mon métier d'actrice en province,
with my acting work out in the regions,

1122
00:51:38,080 --> 00:51:38,660
alors voilà, quoi.
so, there you have it.

1123
00:51:39,820 --> 00:51:40,340
Ah oui.
Oh yes.

1124
00:51:40,740 --> 00:51:42,260
Surtout qu'il faisait hyper humide cet après-midi,
Especially since it was incredibly humid this afternoon,

1125
00:51:42,300 --> 00:51:43,420
donc bonjour les rheumatismes.
so hello, rheumatism.

1126
00:51:44,180 --> 00:51:46,120
Cet après-midi, is this a joke ?
This afternoon — is this a joke?

1127
00:51:46,560 --> 00:51:47,740
Non, c'est-à-dire que...
No, I mean...

1128
00:51:47,740 --> 00:51:50,900
En fait, je veux dire cet après-midi-là,
I mean, that afternoon,

1129
00:51:50,980 --> 00:51:52,840
le jour où on a tourné le film.
the day we shot the film.

1130
00:51:54,050 --> 00:51:55,290
Bon, écoutez, ça suffit maintenant.
Right, that's enough now.

1131
00:51:55,410 --> 00:51:56,890
J'en ai assez de cet interrogatoire.
I've had quite enough of this interrogation.

1132
00:51:56,910 --> 00:51:58,290
On est ici entre grands professionnels
We're all professionals here

1133
00:51:58,290 --> 00:51:59,490
et vous êtes là à nous juger.
and you're sitting there judging us.

1134
00:51:59,490 --> 00:52:00,670
Ça va bien comme ça.
That'll do.

1135
00:52:01,590 --> 00:52:02,290
Isabelle, calmez-vous.
Isabelle, calm down.

1136
00:52:02,410 --> 00:52:03,570
Je vous présente toutes nos excuses.
We sincerely apologize.

1137
00:52:03,710 --> 00:52:04,610
Non, mais écoutez, elle a raison, enfin.
No, but listen, she has a point, really.

1138
00:52:04,810 --> 00:52:05,690
Je vous en supplie, restez.
I beg you, please stay.

1139
00:52:06,130 --> 00:52:07,010
Partez pas. Pardon.
Don't go. I'm sorry.

1140
00:52:07,890 --> 00:52:08,170
Pardon.
I'm sorry.

1141
00:52:09,570 --> 00:52:11,010
Je suis désolée, mais là, je peux pas vous laisser
I'm sorry, but I can't let you

1142
00:52:11,010 --> 00:52:12,510
manquer de respect à son travail comme ça.
disrespect her work like that.

1143
00:52:12,710 --> 00:52:13,950
Mais quel travail ?
What work?

1144
00:52:13,950 --> 00:52:17,630
Enfin, Isabelle est une actrice époustouflante.
I mean, Isabelle is a breathtaking actress.

1145
00:52:17,650 --> 00:52:19,010
Pourquoi ? Parce qu'elle fait du théâtre en province,
What, because she does theater in the provinces,

1146
00:52:19,070 --> 00:52:20,110
alors ça n'existe pas ?
that means she doesn't count?

1147
00:52:20,110 --> 00:52:21,130
Mais qu'est-ce que c'est que ce snobisme ?
What kind of snobbery is that?

1148
00:52:21,710 --> 00:52:23,670
Isabelle était époustouflante
Isabelle was breathtaking

1149
00:52:23,670 --> 00:52:24,870
dans son rôle d'infirmière dans...
in her role as the nurse in...

1150
00:52:26,290 --> 00:52:27,250
Dans soins intensifs.
In Intensive Care.

1151
00:52:27,630 --> 00:52:27,910
Oui.
Yes.

1152
00:52:28,510 --> 00:52:29,990
Je l'ai beaucoup jouée, cette pièce-là.
I performed that play many times.

1153
00:52:30,350 --> 00:52:31,470
Ah, j'adorais le moment
Oh, I loved the moment

1154
00:52:31,950 --> 00:52:33,850
avec le petit monsieur.
with the little old man.

1155
00:52:34,880 --> 00:52:37,220
Vous savez, quand vous entrez dans la chambre du...
You know, when you walk into the room of the...

1156
00:52:37,220 --> 00:52:38,540
Le petit monsieur ?
The little old man?

1157
00:52:38,540 --> 00:52:40,020
Le petit monsieur, c'est la scène...
The little old man — that's the scene...

1158
00:52:40,020 --> 00:52:40,860
Oui, monsieur Cardette.
Yes, Mr. Cardette.

1159
00:52:41,100 --> 00:52:41,320
Oui.
Yes.

1160
00:52:41,460 --> 00:52:42,320
Ah, oui.
Oh, yes.

1161
00:52:42,660 --> 00:52:44,280
Oui, c'est la scène où je...
Yes, it's the scene where I...

1162
00:52:44,780 --> 00:52:47,300
où donc je joue le rôle de l'infirmière.
where I play the role of the nurse.

1163
00:52:48,660 --> 00:52:50,980
Et je fais les soins à ce petit monsieur.
And I'm tending to this little old man.

1164
00:52:51,140 --> 00:52:51,280
Oui.
Yes.

1165
00:52:51,380 --> 00:52:52,660
En fait, il est vieux.
He's very old, actually.

1166
00:52:52,740 --> 00:52:54,700
Il doit avoir 90 ans.
He must be around 90.

1167
00:52:54,860 --> 00:52:56,540
Et il s'est cassé le col du fémur.
And he broke his hip.

1168
00:52:56,880 --> 00:53:00,500
Et donc, je sens qu'il a envie
And I can sense that he wants

1169
00:53:00,500 --> 00:53:00,840
de passer un peu plus de temps
to spend a little more time

1170
00:53:00,860 --> 00:53:00,920
pour lui parler.
just talking.

1171
00:53:01,180 --> 00:53:02,820
Mais moi, j'ai 3 minutes 45
But I only have 3 minutes 45

1172
00:53:02,820 --> 00:53:04,120
pour nettoyer chaque patient.
to attend to each patient.

1173
00:53:04,300 --> 00:53:04,720
J'ai pas le temps.
I don't have time.

1174
00:53:04,840 --> 00:53:05,920
Et je lui dis...
And I say to him...

1175
00:53:05,920 --> 00:53:08,580
À tout à l'heure, en partant.
See you later, as I'm leaving.

1176
00:53:08,640 --> 00:53:08,860
Ah, oui.
Oh, yes.

1177
00:53:09,260 --> 00:53:10,720
Et à la fin de ma journée,
And at the end of my shift,

1178
00:53:12,090 --> 00:53:15,270
j'étais fatiguée et je me dis...
I was tired, and I thought...

1179
00:53:15,270 --> 00:53:17,590
Bon, faut que je repasse le voir quand même.
Right, I should go check on him anyway.

1180
00:53:18,090 --> 00:53:20,700
Et je rentre dans sa chambre
And I go back into his room

1181
00:53:21,420 --> 00:53:23,400
et il était mort.
and he was dead.

1182
00:53:25,670 --> 00:53:26,410
Il est mort.
He died.

1183
00:53:26,830 --> 00:53:29,800
J'ai pas eu le temps de lui parler.
I didn't have time to talk to him.

1184
00:53:33,710 --> 00:53:37,080
Vous êtes encore dans votre personnage ?
Are you still in character?

1185
00:53:38,880 --> 00:53:39,580
Oui, parce qu'il a...
Yes, because he...

1186
00:53:39,580 --> 00:53:40,620
Elle est une très grande actrice,
She is a truly great actress,

1187
00:53:40,680 --> 00:53:41,360
comme je vous l'ai dit.
as I've told you.

1188
00:53:41,400 --> 00:53:41,520
Oui.
Yes.

1189
00:53:42,900 --> 00:53:44,400
Et elle prend ses rôles très à cœur.
And she takes her roles very much to heart.

1190
00:53:44,580 --> 00:53:44,740
Oui.
Yes.

1191
00:53:47,290 --> 00:53:48,330
Pardonnez-moi de vous déranger,
Forgive me for interrupting,

1192
00:53:48,410 --> 00:53:49,110
mais pour le loulou,
but regarding the little one,

1193
00:53:49,110 --> 00:53:50,690
j'aimerais beaucoup s'entretenir avec Isabelle.
I'd very much like to have a word with Isabelle.

1194
00:53:51,350 --> 00:53:51,710
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

1195
00:53:52,830 --> 00:53:54,810
Écoutez, comme j'aime beaucoup ce que vous faites
Listen, I'm a great admirer of your work

1196
00:53:54,810 --> 00:53:56,270
et que je prépare un nouveau film,
and I'm developing a new film —

1197
00:53:56,550 --> 00:53:58,770
j'ai peut-être quelque chose de très intéressant
I may have something very interesting

1198
00:53:58,770 --> 00:53:59,450
à vous proposer.
to offer you.

1199
00:53:59,490 --> 00:54:00,610
Je peux vous parler ?
May I have a word?

1200
00:54:00,900 --> 00:54:01,960
Allez-y, bien sûr.
Please, go ahead.

1201
00:54:03,320 --> 00:54:04,120
Vous permettez ?
May I?

1202
00:54:04,120 --> 00:54:04,580
Of course.
Of course.

1203
00:54:05,280 --> 00:54:06,280
It's such an honor.
It's such an honor.

1204
00:54:06,560 --> 00:54:08,700
J'aime tellement un homme et une femme.
I just love a man and a woman together.

1205
00:54:09,680 --> 00:54:10,040
Merci.
Thank you.

1206
00:54:16,880 --> 00:54:18,460
T'es pas croyable, cette soirée.
You're unbelievable — what a night.

1207
00:54:18,700 --> 00:54:19,060
Non.
No.

1208
00:54:19,080 --> 00:54:20,340
Non, mais c'est vous qui êtes pas croyables.
No, but you two are the unbelievable ones.

1209
00:54:21,920 --> 00:54:24,560
Si jamais j'ai une actrice qui doit jouer une infirmière,
If I ever have an actress who needs to play a nurse,

1210
00:54:24,620 --> 00:54:25,520
je vous l'envoie en stage.
I'll send her to you for training.

1211
00:54:25,840 --> 00:54:27,140
Ah oui, bien sûr.
Oh yes, of course.

1212
00:54:27,440 --> 00:54:29,120
Les filles, elles font souvent n'importe quoi.
Women will do just about anything.

1213
00:54:32,160 --> 00:54:32,520
Bon.
Right.

1214
00:54:34,070 --> 00:54:35,620
Au revoir.
Goodbye.

1215
00:54:37,700 --> 00:54:38,320
Isabelle, merci.
Isabelle, thank you.

1216
00:54:40,250 --> 00:54:41,990
Merci de ce que vous avez fait pour nous.
Thank you for everything you did for us.

1217
00:54:42,880 --> 00:54:44,080
J'étais vraiment très fière
I was truly very proud

1218
00:54:44,080 --> 00:54:45,180
d'être votre agent ce soir.
to be your agent tonight.

1219
00:55:20,070 --> 00:55:21,110
Il est tout là-bas, là.
He's all the way over there.

1220
00:55:22,230 --> 00:55:24,670
Ça va être à vous. Je vais vous chercher un petit verre d'eau.
You're up soon. Let me get you a glass of water.

1221
00:55:26,330 --> 00:55:26,690
Pardon.
Excuse me.

1222
00:55:37,540 --> 00:55:37,860
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

1223
00:55:38,640 --> 00:55:39,720
Il faut que vous veniez.
You have to come.

1224
00:55:39,800 --> 00:55:41,400
Il va y avoir un discours magnifique.
There's going to be a wonderful speech.

1225
00:55:41,760 --> 00:55:42,560
C'est super.
That's great.

1226
00:55:43,380 --> 00:55:44,940
Vous me donnez du champagne, s'il vous plaît ?
Could I get some champagne, please?

1227
00:55:45,560 --> 00:55:45,880
Merci.
Thank you.

1228
00:55:53,660 --> 00:55:54,220
Bonsoir, Monika.
Good evening, Monika.

1229
00:55:57,460 --> 00:55:57,780
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

1230
00:55:59,000 --> 00:56:00,700
Écoute, tu veux pas faire le mec qui fait son bon ?
Look, don't play the righteous guy here.

1231
00:56:00,700 --> 00:56:02,780
J'ai vu ta couverture avec ton milliardaire.
I saw your cover with your billionaire.

1232
00:56:03,240 --> 00:56:04,360
Ces gens sont des trop-morts.
These people are total stiffs.

1233
00:56:05,290 --> 00:56:06,450
Mais je connais un avocat.
But I know a lawyer.

1234
00:56:07,320 --> 00:56:08,180
Si ça t'intéresse.
If you're interested.

1235
00:56:08,920 --> 00:56:09,240
Merci.
Thank you.

1236
00:56:10,470 --> 00:56:11,450
En même temps, je me dis...
Then again, I keep thinking...

1237
00:56:12,150 --> 00:56:13,660
Peut-être que ça te plaît, ce jour-là.
Maybe you actually liked it that day.

1238
00:56:14,600 --> 00:56:15,240
Ma taille.
My figure.

1239
00:56:15,360 --> 00:56:16,740
Je le connais même pas, ce type.
I don't even know the guy.

1240
00:56:17,540 --> 00:56:19,440
En plus, il est pas du tout mon style.
Plus, he's not my type at all.

1241
00:56:20,190 --> 00:56:21,330
C'est quoi, ton style ?
So what is your type?

1242
00:56:23,520 --> 00:56:24,960
Je voudrais juste un mec normal.
I just want a normal guy.

1243
00:56:26,890 --> 00:56:29,360
Ah. Eh bien, t'as pu pour moi.
Ah. Well, guess I'm not your guy.

1244
00:56:30,760 --> 00:56:31,380
Bonsoir, Monika.
Good evening, Monika.

1245
00:56:36,840 --> 00:56:37,300
Joé ?
Joé?

1246
00:56:40,100 --> 00:56:40,760
Bonsoir, tout le monde.
Good evening, everyone.

1247
00:56:41,040 --> 00:56:41,360
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

1248
00:56:42,520 --> 00:56:44,360
Ce soir est un peu électrique, hein ?
Tonight's a bit electric, isn't it?

1249
00:56:45,380 --> 00:56:46,300
Heureusement, il n'y a pas eu de blessés.
Fortunately, no one was hurt.

1250
00:56:47,180 --> 00:56:48,300
Merci d'être venus si nombreux.
Thank you all for coming out in such numbers.

1251
00:56:49,210 --> 00:56:50,430
Ça fait pas 30 ans que je suis là,
I haven't been here 30 years,

1252
00:56:50,430 --> 00:56:52,410
mais assez longtemps pour voir que la réussite à SK, elle est collective.
but long enough to see that success at SK is a team effort.

1253
00:56:53,670 --> 00:56:54,830
Même si chaque agent,
Even though every agent

1254
00:56:54,950 --> 00:56:56,770
on vous dira que tout ça, c'est grâce à lui et lui seul.
will tell you it's all thanks to them and them alone.

1255
00:56:57,640 --> 00:56:58,560
Hein ? Non.
Right? No.

1256
00:56:58,980 --> 00:57:00,760
Il dirait jamais ça, un agent, ça ment pas.
An agent would never say that — agents don't lie.

1257
00:57:01,400 --> 00:57:03,000
SK n'existerait pas sans vous tous.
SK wouldn't exist without all of you.

1258
00:57:03,580 --> 00:57:04,280
Vous, les talents.
You, the talent.

1259
00:57:05,340 --> 00:57:07,240
Mais les talents que j'aimerais mettre à l'honneur ce soir,
But the talent I'd like to celebrate tonight

1260
00:57:08,070 --> 00:57:09,290
ce sont ceux de vos agents.
is that of your agents.

1261
00:57:10,220 --> 00:57:10,960
Merci pour eux.
Thank you on their behalf.

1262
00:57:19,310 --> 00:57:21,470
Il y a une personne qui mérite particulièrement
There is one person who especially deserves

1263
00:57:21,470 --> 00:57:22,410
vos applaudissements ce soir.
your applause this evening.

1264
00:57:23,520 --> 00:57:25,260
Quelqu'un qui incarne véritablement SK.
Someone who truly embodies SK.

1265
00:57:25,560 --> 00:57:27,820
Un agent redouté, redoutable,
A feared, formidable agent,

1266
00:57:28,320 --> 00:57:29,520
qui était là il y a 30 ans.
who was here 30 years ago.

1267
00:57:30,490 --> 00:57:31,590
Là, juste en dessous.
Right down there.

1268
00:57:31,730 --> 00:57:34,450
Dans un petit bureau, avec une petite chaise,
In a small office, with a small chair,

1269
00:57:34,550 --> 00:57:37,490
une petite table, un canapé, et rien d'autre.
a small table, a sofa, and nothing else.

1270
00:57:38,120 --> 00:57:39,480
Aux côtés de Samuel Kerr.
At Samuel Kerr's side.

1271
00:57:41,260 --> 00:57:42,700
La très grande Arlette Azemar.
The great Arlette Azemar.

1272
00:57:43,120 --> 00:57:49,580
Sans elle, on serait pas là ce soir.
Without her, we wouldn't be here tonight.

1273
00:57:50,940 --> 00:57:51,700
Merci, Arlette.
Thank you, Arlette.

1274
00:57:52,080 --> 00:57:53,120
Merci beaucoup.
Thank you very much.

1275
00:57:54,610 --> 00:57:55,470
Voilà, bonne soirée.
And on that note, enjoy your evening.

1276
00:57:56,700 --> 00:57:57,320
Merci à tous.
Thank you all.

1277
00:58:00,360 --> 00:58:01,980
Mesdames, messieurs, je voulais vous informer
Ladies and gentlemen, I wanted to let you know

1278
00:58:01,980 --> 00:58:03,620
que le buffet des desserts est ouvert.
that the dessert buffet is now open.

1279
00:58:04,200 --> 00:58:05,600
Donc, si vous aimez...
So if you'd like...

1280
00:58:12,160 --> 00:58:12,660
C'est pas le moment.
This isn't the time.

1281
00:58:13,820 --> 00:58:15,100
Comment c'est pas le moment ?
What do you mean, not the time?

1282
00:58:15,170 --> 00:58:15,710
Ouais.
Yeah.

1283
00:58:16,940 --> 00:58:18,840
C'est pas très classe d'annoncer devant tout le monde
It's not exactly classy to announce in front of everyone

1284
00:58:18,840 --> 00:58:19,540
que tu vas quitter SK.
that you're leaving SK.

1285
00:58:21,490 --> 00:58:23,330
Tu as sous-estimé tes collègues, Mathias.
You underestimated your colleagues, Mathias.

1286
00:58:25,270 --> 00:58:26,170
Ça a été ton erreur.
That was your mistake.

1287
00:58:26,250 --> 00:58:26,630
Depuis le début.
From the very beginning.

1288
00:58:28,330 --> 00:58:29,970
Parce qu'ils les ont retournés, les Américains.
Because the Americans turned them.

1289
00:58:31,700 --> 00:58:32,060
Voilà.
There you go.

1290
00:58:33,120 --> 00:58:34,140
Tu t'as joué, t'as perdu.
You played, you lost.

1291
00:59:11,940 --> 00:59:12,820
Je savais pas.
I didn't know.

1292
00:59:12,840 --> 00:59:14,000
J'étais pas au courant, je te promets.
I wasn't in the loop, I swear.

1293
00:59:14,740 --> 00:59:15,580
T'inquiète pas.
Don't worry about it.

1294
00:59:16,860 --> 00:59:17,600
Tu vas où ?
Where are you going?

1295
00:59:17,600 --> 00:59:18,480
Tu vas faire quoi ?
What are you going to do?

1296
00:59:20,820 --> 00:59:21,380
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

1297
00:59:22,730 --> 00:59:23,690
Faire l'agent ailleurs.
Work as an agent somewhere else.

1298
00:59:25,730 --> 00:59:27,070
Tu veux venir avec moi ?
Do you want to come with me?

1299
00:59:27,620 --> 00:59:29,140
Tu auras besoin d'un agent junior.
You'll need a junior agent.

1300
00:59:34,850 --> 00:59:35,550
Je suis désolée.
I'm sorry.

1301
00:59:35,610 --> 00:59:36,610
Je crois que j'aimerais bien rester ici.
I think I'd like to stay here.

1302
00:59:37,640 --> 00:59:38,640
S'ils veulent bien me garder.
If they'll have me.

1303
00:59:39,240 --> 00:59:40,780
Évidemment qu'ils vont bien vouloir te garder.
Of course they'll have you.

1304
00:59:41,340 --> 00:59:43,380
T'es doué.
You're talented.

1305
00:59:45,040 --> 00:59:46,520
T'es quelqu'un de bien, Camille.
You're a good person, Camille.

1306
00:59:46,820 --> 00:59:56,500
Elle est fine.
She's sharp.

1307
00:59:56,880 --> 01:00:22,460
Pas de monde au péché.
No crowd at confession.

1308
01:00:22,940 --> 01:00:23,960
Je sais pas, tu fais quoi ?
I don't know, what are you going to do?

1309
01:00:26,180 --> 01:00:29,040
Quand tu vas le suivre, t'es pas obligée.
When you go after him, you don't have to.

1310
01:00:30,100 --> 01:00:31,040
Ça lui ferait les pieds.
It'd serve him right.

1311
01:00:36,420 --> 01:00:46,400
Écoute, Hervé, tu sais, Philippe,
Listen, Hervé, you know, Philippe —

1312
01:00:48,140 --> 01:00:49,660
en fait, c'est Mathias.
actually, it's Mathias.

1313
01:00:59,410 --> 01:01:00,350
Vas-y, je suis en veille.
Go ahead, I'm on standby.

1314
01:01:26,290 --> 01:01:29,740
Quand même, ça va faire bizarre ici sans Mathias.
Still, it's going to feel strange here without Mathias.

1315
01:01:31,390 --> 01:01:32,930
Il m'a fait de la peine un petit peu tout à l'heure.
He made me feel a little sorry for him just now.

1316
01:01:34,570 --> 01:01:34,930
Ouais.
Yeah.

1317
01:01:36,940 --> 01:01:38,180
Pour un peu, il nous manquerait.
Almost makes you miss him.

1318
01:01:41,650 --> 01:01:42,410
Bon, j'y vais.
Right, I'm heading out.

1319
01:01:43,160 --> 01:01:44,360
Tu pourras fermer la boutique.
Can you lock up?

1320
01:01:44,620 --> 01:01:45,640
Pas de problème.
No problem.

1321
01:01:45,940 --> 01:01:50,240
Tu pourrais t'occuper de la boutique tout court.
You could just run the shop, full stop.

1322
01:01:52,990 --> 01:01:54,650
J'ai décidé de passer plus de temps à Londres.
I've decided to spend more time in London.

1323
01:01:55,010 --> 01:01:55,990
Mon fils a besoin de moi.
My son needs me.

1324
01:01:57,580 --> 01:01:59,940
Et moi, j'ai besoin de quelqu'un de confiance en commande quand je suis pas là.
And I need someone I trust in charge when I'm not around.

1325
01:02:00,940 --> 01:02:01,560
Un DG.
A GM.

1326
01:02:03,120 --> 01:02:04,260
Ça t'intéresse ?
Interested?

1327
01:02:33,230 --> 01:02:33,690
Sophia ?
Sophia?

1328
01:02:34,210 --> 01:02:34,750
Ouais ?
Yeah?

1329
01:02:34,750 --> 01:02:36,010
Tu décroches, s'il te plaît ?
Can you pick up, please?

1330
01:02:36,620 --> 01:02:38,180
Il est 4h du mat', là, c'est bon.
It's 4 in the morning, come on.

1331
01:02:38,740 --> 01:02:40,300
Bah, c'est toi qui reprends l'accueil, non ?
Well, you're the one taking over reception, aren't you?

1332
01:02:41,060 --> 01:02:41,580
Excuse-moi.
Excuse me.

1333
01:02:48,080 --> 01:02:49,280
Ah, est-ce qu'à bonjour ?
Ah, hello— is this a good—

1334
01:02:49,660 --> 01:02:55,920
Bonjour, je souhaite vous communiquer la liste des nommés pour la cérémonie des Césars.
Good morning, I'd like to inform you of the nominees for the César ceremony.

1335
01:02:57,530 --> 01:02:59,750
C'est très sympa, mais il est tard un peu, là.
That's very kind, but it's a bit late, isn't it?

1336
01:02:59,830 --> 01:03:00,250
Quand même, non ?
All the same, no?

1337
01:03:00,670 --> 01:03:02,030
Faut dormir, les gens, dans ce métier.
People need to sleep in this business.

1338
01:03:02,700 --> 01:03:06,730
Alors, dans la catégorie révélation féminine,
So, in the category of Best New Actress,

1339
01:03:07,430 --> 01:03:12,650
est nommée Sophia Leprince pour son rôle dans l'Océan Jouy de Julien Dor...
nominated is Sophia Leprince for her role in Julien Dor's L'Océan Jouy...

1340
01:03:13,780 --> 01:03:14,780
Pardon ?
I beg your pardon?

1341
01:03:15,680 --> 01:03:17,520
Vous êtes nommée Sophia Leprince ?
You're nominated, Sophia Leprince?

1342
01:03:17,520 --> 01:03:22,200
Ramelle, tout à l'heure, c'est vrai que c'est...
Ramelle, earlier, it's true that it's...

1343
01:03:23,910 --> 01:03:24,470
Félicitations.
Congratulations.

1344
01:03:25,740 --> 01:03:27,960
Gabrielle, je suis nommée aux Césars ?
Gabrielle, I'm nominated at the Césars?

1345
01:03:28,670 --> 01:03:29,190
Non.
No.

1346
01:03:32,410 --> 01:03:34,690
Dans mes bras, ma poulette !
Come here, sweetheart!

1347
01:03:34,690 --> 01:03:36,150
Meilleur espoir féminin.
Best New Actress.

1348
01:03:36,470 --> 01:03:37,510
Mais c'est la classe !
That's so cool!

1349
01:03:38,470 --> 01:03:39,030
Merci, Arlette.
Thank you, Arlette.

1350
01:03:40,010 --> 01:03:41,570
Mais si c'est maintenant, on dit révélation.
Well, now they call it "revelation," not "new actress."

1351
01:03:42,720 --> 01:03:44,060
Je vais vous faire dire espoir.
I'll make you say "espoir."

1352
01:03:44,340 --> 01:03:45,200
C'est plus joli.
It sounds prettier.

1353
01:03:46,440 --> 01:04:12,110
On va pas se laisser faire, hein.
We're not going to take this lying down.

1354
01:04:12,670 --> 01:04:15,100
Vous allez voir, on va rebondir.
You'll see, we're going to bounce back.

1355
01:04:16,170 --> 01:04:17,930
Et on va voir, tous, là, de quoi on est capables.
And we'll all see what we're made of.

1356
01:04:18,230 --> 01:04:18,690
Hein ?
Right?

1357
01:04:19,150 --> 01:04:20,730
Vous avez toujours un coup d'avance, vous ?
Always one step ahead, aren't you?

1358
01:04:20,730 --> 01:04:23,850
Vous trouvez pas que c'est excitant, ce qui se passe ?
Don't you find what's happening exciting?

1359
01:04:24,350 --> 01:04:26,890
Y a quelque chose qui s'ouvre, là. Non ?
Something's opening up here. Don't you think?

1360
01:04:32,660 --> 01:04:33,240
T'as raison.
You're right.

1361
01:04:33,460 --> 01:04:37,370
On se tutoie, maintenant ?
Are we on first-name terms now?

1362
01:04:37,370 --> 01:04:40,050
C'est un nouveau départ, non ?
It's a fresh start, isn't it?
